          "content": {
            "mimeType": "application/json; charset=utf-8",
            "size": 45655,
            "text": "{\"result\":[{\"content\":[{\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"fa443d35f0fc\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"text\":\"Synopsis\",\"_key\":\"76d161bf32d7\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}],\"_type\":\"block\"},{\"_key\":\"0e8749677077\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"The Adaptation Atlas’ climate risk and response data helps IUCN’s develop clear reasoning and justification to shape their livestock-centric Green Climate Fund proposal.\\n\\n\",\"_key\":\"0849fc1de107\"},{\"text\":\"Use Case:\",\"_key\":\"46c034cd7452\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"]},{\"_key\":\"16caf233015c\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" Surfacing climate and adaptation data to inform climate-responsive proposals\\n\"},{\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Stakeholder Group:\",\"_key\":\"d03d6246e679\",\"_type\":\"span\"},{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" NGO\\n\",\"_key\":\"3b6ea2486063\",\"_type\":\"span\"},{\"text\":\"Impact:\",\"_key\":\"1578e17af9a2\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"]},{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" Unlocking finance\\n\",\"_key\":\"ef1ebe3c2784\",\"_type\":\"span\"},{\"text\":\"KPI:\",\"_key\":\"f44159091964\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"]},{\"text\":\" US$34 Million\\n\",\"_key\":\"43f2c0f9279c\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]},{\"_key\":\"5bae7760f844\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Geography:\"},{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" United Republic of Tanzania\",\"_key\":\"6f542d23520f\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\"},{\"_type\":\"imageFull\",\"alt\":\"Farmland with livestock\",\"caption\":[{\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"b968562e274a\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Image credit:\",\"_key\":\"ad109f61c47b\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" ©2014CCAFS/C Schubert\",\"_key\":\"576bd8beba65\"}],\"_type\":\"block\"}],\"_key\":\"ea2e5149d073\",\"asset\":{\"_ref\":\"image-3ae14a83b579961ff71b1a319952e61e8e34e845-1560x891-jpg\",\"_type\":\"reference\"}},{\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"3b56b92a8e600\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Rapid and robust data\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"570994e7ea15\",\"markDefs\":[]},{\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"61a3e6437068\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"text\":\"When the Government of the United Republic of Tanzania decided to prioritize livestock keepers in its next Green Climate Fund proposal due to the vulnerability and economic significance of the sector, the International Union for Conservation of Nature (IUCN) aligned its efforts to support this direction. The Adaptation Atlas, with its unique mix of climate risk and livestock data, became crucial support for this transition.\",\"_key\":\"a1eead53c0190\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}],\"_type\":\"block\"},{\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"61cec8661df9\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"text\":\"Utilizing the data, IUCN and partners rapidly understood the risks to livestock production posed by climate change, including the historical climate trends and potential for future anomalies as well as the production vulnerability. These data were vital in building a strong case for a new livestock-focused project, illustrating the extent of production at risk and the economic value under threat. It enabled IUCN to present a data-driven narrative, effectively highlighting the urgency and importance of focusing on livestock within Tanzania’s adaptation strategy.\",\"_key\":\"5d682cd2b13e0\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}],\"_type\":\"block\"},{\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"c7b80aca0d96\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Thanks to the detailed insights from the Atlas’ data, IUCN delivered robust climate rationale for the livestock initiative, aligning with the Tanzanian government’s objectives and responding to the country's needs with targeted, evidence-based actions. The Adaptation Atlas Team facilitated a rapid response and underscored the importance of adapting actions for livestock in Tanzania’s response to the climate crisis.\",\"_key\":\"eb6c778875960\",\"_type\":\"span\"}]},{\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"8d61bdfb905f0\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Partners\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"3812f699ed89\",\"markDefs\":[]},{\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"International Union for the Conservation of Nature (IUCN); Alliance of Bioversity-CIAT\",\"_key\":\"5b0e36c721f0\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"4a53686e2bce\",\"markDefs\":[]}],\"_id\":\"1371e7ea-bbfc-4dbe-9034-dfcbf5719cdc\",\"_type\":\"impact\",\"title\":\"IUCN develops climate rationale for Green Climate Fund proposal with Atlas climate projections and  livestock data\",\"slug\":\"iucn-gcf\"},{\"content\":[{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"text\":\"Synopsis\",\"_key\":\"6f055d1a4b41\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"]}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"01b271749a68\"},{\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"fce8a4d86720\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"A workshop with 40+ participants demonstrated the need for value chain-specific gender metrics. The insights fed into discussions around Malawi’s National Resilience Strategy discussions. During the workshop, researchers expressed interest in Atlas datasets for new adaptation-focused studies. Moreover, early engagement with development partners created openings for support on climate-smart agriculture pilots. Malawi’s Ministry of Agriculture, and its Department of Climate Change and Meteorological Services signaled intent to use Atlas evidence in district planning.\",\"_key\":\"6052d3dee87a\"}]},{\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"84aacf5d9d30\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Stakeholder Group:\",\"_key\":\"0505e16febcb\"},{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" University, Governmental Agency, Farmer Organization, NGO\\n\",\"_key\":\"e2b496fbc5c9\",\"_type\":\"span\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Impact: \",\"_key\":\"2224b7dac60d\"},{\"text\":\"Identify data and research needs\\n\",\"_key\":\"05e5f9cd19f9\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Geography: \",\"_key\":\"b42a991b3d71\"},{\"_key\":\"2df7590048e0\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Malawi\"}],\"_type\":\"block\"},{\"_type\":\"imageFull\",\"caption\":[{\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"01616acfbee6\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Image credit:\",\"_key\":\"b6831f1fcfac\",\"_type\":\"span\"},{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" © CIAT\",\"_key\":\"16ec83c92cfb\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"_type\":\"block\"}],\"_key\":\"63546ef56be9\",\"asset\":{\"_type\":\"reference\",\"_ref\":\"image-e6a891dcf30dbfd21e70d8b7cef29d294e079ad5-2048x1360-jpg\"}},{\"children\":[{\"text\":\"Partners:\",\"_key\":\"368aad6b4338\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"]},{\"text\":\" Lilongwe University of Agriculture and Natural Resources (LUANAR), Malawi Ministry of Agriculture, Department of Climate Change and Meteorological Services (DCCMS), Local farmer organizations, NGOs\",\"_key\":\"5a05bc8c4231\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"222ef0a719e8\",\"markDefs\":[]}],\"_id\":\"1e408398-57fa-4ae4-93e0-1dfb237fb572\",\"_type\":\"impact\",\"title\":\"Conducting a cost-benefit analysis of banana value chain interventions supported by Malawi’s Ministry of Agriculture\",\"slug\":\"malawi-banana-interventions\"},{\"content\":[{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Synopsis\",\"_key\":\"a591c5f22c45\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"b83008384b37\"},{\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"162621ddaf2e\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"215a7b6e1d25\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"This case study combined data from the National Integrated Agriculture Survey (IAI) with the Atlas platform to analyze levels of CSA adoption and their effects on maize yields in Mozambique. Atlas notebooks such as ‘Evaluate Climate Risks’, ‘Projected Climate Impacts’, and ‘Discover Solutions’ were applied to generate adaptation recommendations under different emission scenarios. A gender-disaggregated lens was also incorporated to assess differences in CSA adoption and benefits between male- and female-headed households.\"}],\"_type\":\"block\"},{\"_key\":\"4141cc0fc3d7\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"The analysis demonstrated that irrigation and organic fertilization deliver the largest maize yield gains, with Atlas projections reinforcing these results by showing potential increases of up to 0.98 ton/ha. It also highlighted gender-differentiated benefits, such as women farmers benefiting more from mulching while men benefited more from irrigation and zero tillage. Beyond the field-level findings, the work strengthened institutional capacity to use Atlas evidence within Mozambique’s CSA Guidelines and policy frameworks, aligning with national strategies such as NAPA, ENAMMC (2013–2025), and the National Adaptation Plan (2023). The Atlas was thereby positioned as a tool for supporting decentralized adaptation planning and informing agricultural investment strategies.\",\"_key\":\"b4f0386b99d8\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\"},{\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"55154dd06763\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Stakeholder Group:\",\"_key\":\"bb8e3a743dd9\"},{\"text\":\" Research Organization, Governmental Agency, NGO, Academia, Technology\\n\",\"_key\":\"617fa387d43e\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]},{\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Impact:\",\"_key\":\"84eb6bc27190\",\"_type\":\"span\"},{\"_key\":\"be0c5ee28eda\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" Decentralize adaptation planning and inform agricultural investment strategies\\n\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Geography:\",\"_key\":\"4914b51d652e\"},{\"_key\":\"87e5d42d5e6b\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" Mozambique\"}],\"_type\":\"block\"},{\"_type\":\"imageFull\",\"caption\":[{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"text\":\"Image credit: \",\"_key\":\"eac5459e1cb4\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"]},{\"_key\":\"0b2249aab4b9\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"©2016 CIAT/NeilPalmer\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"4b3dfbfa0dab\"}],\"_key\":\"323a73a21a03\",\"asset\":{\"_ref\":\"image-3d896879184e949a0ff7519d2af7c9b6a4d3c642-1600x1068-jpg\",\"_type\":\"reference\"}},{\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"1d7da89f5a08\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Partners:\",\"_key\":\"21673fdc34be\"},{\"_key\":\"c3e103a96ae2\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" Centre of Excellence on Agri-Food Systems and Nutrition (CE-AFSN), Mozambican Ministry of Agriculture’s Climate Change Directorate, Mozambican Ministry of Planning and Economy, Development agencies, Academia, Civil society organizations, Technology developers\"}],\"_type\":\"block\"}],\"_id\":\"5030b380-1a43-4118-8f2f-82f56f667f0b\",\"_type\":\"impact\",\"title\":\"Evaluating the adoption of Climate-Smart Agriculture (CSA) practices and their impacts on maize yields in Mozambique with a gender lens\",\"slug\":\"mozambique-gender-maize\"},{\"title\":\"Using the Atlas to support small-scale irrigation planning in Rwanda and evaluate its effect on productivity and income\",\"slug\":\"rwanda-irrigation-support\",\"content\":[{\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"41635f1fd1bf\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"08998277dfad\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Synopsis\"}]},{\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"e39128e2ba23\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"1fff1f396cc4\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Engagement with Rwanda’s Ministry of Agriculture and Animal Resources (MINAGRI) and the Rwanda Agriculture and Animal Resources Board (RAB) informed ongoing discussions on scaling up small-scale irrigation technologies (SSIT) adoption as part of the country's agricultural adaptation strategies. There was strong agreement between implementing agencies to participate in Atlas trainings, ensuring the integration of the tool into planning. Other institutions expressed interest in developing joint proposals based on Atlas outputs.\"}]},{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"text\":\"Stakeholder Group: \",\"_key\":\"dc545928266b\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"]},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Research Organization, Governmental Agency\\n\",\"_key\":\"240c79c45d66\"},{\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Impact: \",\"_key\":\"67c041f656a9\",\"_type\":\"span\"},{\"_key\":\"3c070571dcbd\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Integrate the Atlas in irrigation planning and proposal writing\\n\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Geography:\",\"_key\":\"ad1d5fbad2bf\"},{\"_key\":\"def95a186366\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" Rwanda\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"e4b67215eea6\"},{\"asset\":{\"_ref\":\"image-f05cb5d74ecce26a23ceb9cd48b5897e1487f0cf-2048x1365-jpg\",\"_type\":\"reference\"},\"_type\":\"imageFull\",\"caption\":[{\"_key\":\"d7e37dacb7b0\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Image Credit:\",\"_key\":\"ecb82ad5f56c\",\"_type\":\"span\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" ©2022 CIAT/Owen Kimani\",\"_key\":\"f17cbbb17ad2\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\"}],\"_key\":\"9440730142e8\"},{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"0bdb0bbc33c1\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Partners:\"},{\"text\":\" Economic Policy Research Network (EPRN Rwanda), Ministry of Agriculture and Animal Resources (MINAGRI), Rwanda Agriculture and Animal Resources Board (RAB)\",\"_key\":\"45ac54423308\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"917c76dc2406\"}],\"_id\":\"573a14f0-10fe-4ad3-889e-0f67517bd1ae\",\"_type\":\"impact\"},{\"_type\":\"impact\",\"title\":\"Applying the Atlas to evaluate the efficiency of banana value interventions by the Tanzanian Ministry of Agriculture\",\"slug\":\"tanzania-intervention-efficiency\",\"content\":[{\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"42d047ae2877\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Synopsis\",\"_key\":\"0272a21ae767\"}],\"_type\":\"block\"},{\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"3255881f46fe\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"text\":\"As a result of a 50+ person workshop in Dar es Salaam, government institutions (MoA, MLF, VPO, NEMC) showed interest in integrating the Atlas into climate adaptation planning. The BBT program was linked with Atlas data to inform youth-focused agri-programming. The training also increased demand for more tailored Atlas sessions for ministries and local governments. The Sokoine University of Agriculture (SUA) and partners began tailoring Atlas data to sunflower seed production and irrigation-focused use cases, with FGDs ensuring gender and inclusivity considerations.\",\"_key\":\"ce30aa07afcc\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}]},{\"_key\":\"82990ff42491\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Stakeholder Group:\",\"_key\":\"a876c47a857f\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" Academia\\n\",\"_key\":\"473b9e6245a8\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Impact:\",\"_key\":\"328b71743001\"},{\"_key\":\"aabf5012213c\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" Use Atlas data to assess intervention effectiveness\\n\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Geography:\",\"_key\":\"d5ee7047c27b\"},{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" Tanzania\",\"_key\":\"a0a39036b9f3\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\"},{\"caption\":[{\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"e8d1c6a300ab\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Image Credit:\"},{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" ©2014 CIAT/GeorginaSmith\",\"_key\":\"7b78c7b22c3a\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"3bbcf9f02807\",\"markDefs\":[]}],\"_key\":\"d420bb9e3ae2\",\"asset\":{\"_ref\":\"image-848af40facfeb4b86cfa5159a8d15a3f250a821d-2048x1360-jpg\",\"_type\":\"reference\"},\"_type\":\"imageFull\"},{\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"a2013bb96bd9\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Partners: \",\"_key\":\"438df92cb3d8\",\"_type\":\"span\"},{\"text\":\"Sokoine University of Agriculture\",\"_key\":\"0d01edc1228b\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}],\"_type\":\"block\"}],\"_id\":\"5796eae9-7e3e-4a92-a46d-9043269b19e5\"},{\"_id\":\"59faa8f5-919f-479c-af5c-dc995c03f8ef\",\"_type\":\"impact\",\"title\":\"Integrating the Atlas into climate policy-making processes across Africa, with a focus on LT-LEDS, NAPs, and NDCs, as well as enhancing parliamentary oversight and gender mainstreaming\",\"slug\":\"africa-climate-policy\",\"content\":[{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"text\":\"Synopsis\",\"_key\":\"059587ee09f4\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"]}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"8d0e301ea760\"},{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Policy stakeholders and civil society were engaged in Kenya and Ghana to deploy multi-level training evaluation tools, develop new notebook concepts, and plan regional sensitization events.\",\"_key\":\"3a87967c896a\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"ff1daa4b49d2\"},{\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"86fb32408471\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Stakeholder Group:\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" Policy, Civil Society\\n\",\"_key\":\"8bc1c5ec3b73\"},{\"_key\":\"e8eaaa47fee6\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Impact:\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" Integrate Atlas into Pan-African climate policy-making processes\\n\",\"_key\":\"a7db38ea778b\"},{\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Geography: \",\"_key\":\"291998ab264e\",\"_type\":\"span\"},{\"_key\":\"2b35facc438d\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Across Africa\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"d4583d22bb63\",\"markDefs\":[]},{\"caption\":[{\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"e21742b87271\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Image Credit:\",\"_key\":\"61125fda1f4d\",\"_type\":\"span\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" ©2014 CIAT/GeorginaSmith\",\"_key\":\"84ecf90847c9\"}],\"_type\":\"block\"}],\"_key\":\"e570fcad0756\",\"asset\":{\"_ref\":\"image-62039622a2d08eab8b1b3d66a2ec381a976ac9a4-2048x1342-jpg\",\"_type\":\"reference\"},\"_type\":\"imageFull\"},{\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"2f1096f2b018\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Partners: \"},{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"AGNES, Kenyan policy stakeholders and civil society\",\"_key\":\"1950e0b3b37e\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"da04f7531b41\",\"markDefs\":[]}]},{\"slug\":\"cgiar-strategy\",\"content\":[{\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"102facb1812a\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"text\":\"Synopsis\",\"_key\":\"dce136513c110\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}]},{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"The Adaptation Atlas geospatial data and analytics engine supported the projection of climate risks and adaptation benefits for CGIAR’s 2022-2030 portfolio, as well as the prioritization process of three initiatives.\\n\\n\",\"_key\":\"640325b6ea4b\"},{\"text\":\"Use Case:\",\"_key\":\"cfa6ee4421f0\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"]},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" Climate data and adaptation analytics that inform projecting the benefits of adaptation research\\n\",\"_key\":\"ddde558d269e\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Stakeholder Group:\",\"_key\":\"0a6e1989ca84\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" Research\\n\",\"_key\":\"d4aad93e5aa6\"},{\"_key\":\"288d73dd4a02\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Impact:\"},{\"_key\":\"258e7dc5dc30\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" Inform strategy\\n\"},{\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"KPIs:\",\"_key\":\"d4456f9c0d53\",\"_type\":\"span\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" 1 (out of 5) long-term strategic action area goals informed, 7 (out of 34 in the whole portfolio of initiatives) initiatives priorities informed, US$ 175M investment informed\\n\",\"_key\":\"701c6dcde187\"},{\"_key\":\"1a7ee23758d5\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Location:\"},{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" Global\",\"_key\":\"4f1f1830e130\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"9ffd8e591a1a\"},{\"asset\":{\"_type\":\"reference\",\"_ref\":\"image-c776f67a3374e16dee5f8ff7262c363437e20372-1280x850-jpg\"},\"_type\":\"imageFull\",\"alt\":\"Investments across various parts of the food systems and in digital technologies for scaling will be crucial to realize sustainable development goals.\",\"caption\":[{\"_key\":\"7ca9dcd33b15\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Image credit:\",\"_key\":\"17ee78d9c43e\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" ©2011CIAT/NeilPalmer\",\"_key\":\"3f599d4a44ce\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\"}],\"_key\":\"37b37355eb6a\"},{\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"da18dbb04ae6\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"text\":\"Evidence-based priority setting\",\"_key\":\"92dcc4838ad40\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}]},{\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"b0a70bfbc182\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"The CGIAR embarked in a process of developing a unified framework for governance and research in 2021. The OneCGIAR (as the unified framework is termed) brought new approaches — and a doubling of investment — with the goal of raising ambition toward achieving the Sustainable Development Goals by 2030. A more integrated and impactful CGIAR included a fresh portfolio of Initiatives to deliver a new 10-year strategy. One of five CGIAR’s impact areas is Climate Adaptation \\u0026 Mitigation.\",\"_key\":\"f1199136c7e20\"}],\"_type\":\"block\"},{\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"The Adaptation Atlas data and modeling methods played an important role in two CGIAR processes. First and foremost, the Adaptation Atlas was instrumental in providing estimations of projected beneficiaries by 2030 from CGIAR’s climate adaptation innovations (\",\"_key\":\"13eacdc6cc260\",\"_type\":\"span\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"86dbfe5c2d9e\"],\"text\":\"Ramirez-Villegas et al., 2021\",\"_key\":\"13eacdc6cc261\"},{\"text\":\"). These estimations were derived from an analysis of rural population exposure to climate hazards in Low- and Middle-Income Countries (LMICs) as well as an analysis (akin to the one in our \",\"_key\":\"13eacdc6cc262\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"3b82f6dd8b04\"],\"text\":\"What’s at Risk?\",\"_key\":\"13eacdc6cc263\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" notebook) as well as an analysis of the productivity benefits of agronomic management options (as in our \",\"_key\":\"13eacdc6cc264\"},{\"marks\":[\"7a62a60e3b2f\"],\"text\":\"On-farm Solutions for Today\",\"_key\":\"13eacdc6cc265\",\"_type\":\"span\"},{\"text\":\" notebook). These estimations provided a clear target for CGIAR to set its ambition in terms of climate adaptation goals.\",\"_key\":\"13eacdc6cc266\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"4ee13781ea9f\",\"markDefs\":[{\"_type\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://hdl.handle.net/10568/115780\",\"_key\":\"86dbfe5c2d9e\"},{\"_type\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://observablehq.com/d/d8c0692154e6c87e#comment-e7f44abeb2263bd2\",\"_key\":\"3b82f6dd8b04\"},{\"_type\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://observablehq.com/d/7539fd16f4fc40e3\",\"_key\":\"7a62a60e3b2f\"}]},{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"The second use of Adaptation Atlas data was to inform design decisions for seven CGIAR initiatives (out of a portfolio of 34). These design decisions were primarily about prioritizing countries and/or farming systems in which initiatives should work. The seven initiatives informed amount to a total of 175M in CGIAR funding, as follows,\",\"_key\":\"1b1c96d6cbd9\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"bc8794414473\"},{\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"5ea3dacdccee\",\"listItem\":\"bullet\",\"markDefs\":[{\"_key\":\"49363508ceee\",\"_type\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://hdl.handle.net/10568/113289\"}],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"The climate and geographic priorities of the five Regional Integrated Initiatives were informed through an analysis of climate hazard exposure, as well as a rapid analysis of crop yield projections under future climates (see \",\"_key\":\"074b2d52df6e0\",\"_type\":\"span\"},{\"_key\":\"074b2d52df6e1\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"49363508ceee\"],\"text\":\"Jarvis et al., 2021\"},{\"text\":\").\",\"_key\":\"074b2d52df6e2\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}],\"level\":1,\"_type\":\"block\"},{\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"da43462e7768\",\"listItem\":\"bullet\",\"markDefs\":[{\"_type\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://observablehq.com/d/9ca8f47f84c8d475\",\"_key\":\"c8e4ffc6773e\"},{\"href\":\"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41893-023-01161-1\",\"_key\":\"b593c3a84f51\",\"_type\":\"link\"}],\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"df4cbee080c20\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"The Livestock \\u0026 Climate initiative’s country and action priorities were informed through an extended (global) version of the \"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"c8e4ffc6773e\"],\"text\":\"Prioritizing Livestock Investments \",\"_key\":\"df4cbee080c21\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"notebook. A key output of this analysis is a publication in the journal Nature Sustainability (\",\"_key\":\"df4cbee080c22\"},{\"marks\":[\"b593c3a84f51\"],\"text\":\"Bonilla-Cedrez et al., 2023\",\"_key\":\"df4cbee080c23\",\"_type\":\"span\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\").\",\"_key\":\"df4cbee080c24\"}],\"level\":1},{\"listItem\":\"bullet\",\"markDefs\":[{\"_type\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10olsWGQp2Z0nHsZXqQpeV0VKhq2TNKY6/view?usp=share_link\",\"_key\":\"6f6d37a5cadd\"}],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"An analysis of crop performance and socioeconomic conditions at the farming system (see \",\"_key\":\"8301578aeecd0\"},{\"_key\":\"8301578aeecd1\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"6f6d37a5cadd\"],\"text\":\"Ghosh et al., 2021\"},{\"_key\":\"8301578aeecd2\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\") level helped inform the priorities of the Excellence in Agronomy initiative.\"}],\"level\":1,\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"9965060d6716\"},{\"_key\":\"1002cfbea17a\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"The existing data and analytics, as well as the responsiveness of the Adaptation Atlas Team to extend Atlas’ analyses beyond Sub-Saharan Africa, quickly package insights, and iteratively engage in the design processes of the CGIAR portfolio during 2021 was crucial in successfully leveraging the Atlas for decision-making.\",\"_key\":\"716fb26c30f50\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\"},{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Partners\",\"_key\":\"8c883df82ace0\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"5ca21d5bb879\"},{\"_key\":\"36a0778843c6\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"text\":\"CGIAR; Alliance of Bioversity-CIAT; IFPRI; IITA\",\"_key\":\"98fb594897e90\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\"}],\"_id\":\"627c2e89-15d9-4aab-9ada-b86cd2580265\",\"_type\":\"impact\",\"title\":\"CGIAR takes strategic research portfolio decisions with Atlas’ hazard and response analytics \"},{\"content\":[{\"_key\":\"f5a6aae6ad03\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"1014b9346f7b\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Synopsis\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\"},{\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"90c92d95bbe6\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"text\":\"Within the scope of a workshop in Accra with 60+ participants, the Atlas helped in strengthening local awareness of Ghana’s Nationally Determined Contributions (NDCs) and National Adaptation Plans (NAPs) by contextualizing them into district-level planning. Atlas data contributed evidence to ongoing discussions under Ghana’s Climate-Smart Agriculture Investment Plan (CSAIP) and enhanced the prioritization of environmental protection policies. The workshop encouraged the integration of gender and social inclusion (GESI) concerns, particularly impacts of mining on education, health, and vulnerable groups.\",\"_key\":\"1909107415a1\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}]},{\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"5d6ddfae8bca\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Use Case: \",\"_key\":\"9ac57b760f99\"},{\"text\":\"Empowering local governance with actionable information on adaptation options for climate action\\n\",\"_key\":\"2458951ab48b\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]},{\"text\":\"Stakeholder Group:\",\"_key\":\"4b1cbc829d23\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"]},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" University, Research Organization, Governmental Agency\\nImpact: Inform policy and investment\\n\",\"_key\":\"469e06c75d3d\"},{\"_key\":\"b9d931e0063c\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Geography:\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" Ghana\",\"_key\":\"8fef2dc06ff5\"}],\"_type\":\"block\"},{\"asset\":{\"_ref\":\"image-ffb0af5eb5e2ced9ae71ac37fce3306db67ff771-2048x1360-jpg\",\"_type\":\"reference\"},\"_type\":\"imageFull\",\"caption\":[{\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"1f4055162145\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"a657b18a7d0e\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Image credit: \"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"©2010 CIAT/NeilPalmer\",\"_key\":\"084bf753ce31\"}]}],\"_key\":\"8fa5e7c4dcaf\"},{\"children\":[{\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"\",\"_key\":\"1d0998789f14\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"2759f524ccf9\",\"markDefs\":[]},{\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"fef7e180cfce\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Partners:\",\"_key\":\"92a2a769566f\",\"_type\":\"span\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" University of Ghana, Agricultural Policy Research Centre (APRC), Council for Scientific and Industrial Research (CSIR) – Crops Research Institute, Ministry of Food and Agriculture (MoFA)\",\"_key\":\"df1e3a0111df\"}]}],\"_id\":\"69bd9a18-9050-4d5f-90c1-eff8f1069114\",\"_type\":\"impact\",\"title\":\"Coalition led by University of Ghana evaluates agroforestry and soil health interventions to reduce heat stress impacts on maize and cocoa farmers\",\"slug\":\"ghana-agroforestry\"},{\"_id\":\"75429f7b-317d-4d5e-84bd-6e323f33c3bc\",\"_type\":\"impact\",\"title\":\"Enhancing the capacity of Kenyan county officers in navigating and utilizing the Atlas, strengthen the integration of climate adaptation into local planning, and co-develop knowledge products tailored to county needs\",\"slug\":\"kenya-county-integration\",\"content\":[{\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"dec3025b6fa4\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"d0413af6d642\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Synopsis\"}],\"_type\":\"block\"},{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Following two-day workshops in each of the 38 counties with 230+ participants, key insights on climate-smart practices such as alternative feeding were updated to inform the refinement of localized knowledge products. This ignited county-level innovations in knowledge product development and showed a need for ongoing support to mainstream climate adaptation into governance systems.\",\"_key\":\"5550902c361b\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"9e96aeb9c922\"},{\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"24d62d0b1374\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Stakeholder Group: \",\"_key\":\"a1ac78e8d800\",\"_type\":\"span\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Governmental Agency\\n\",\"_key\":\"6bc86f4e0a70\"},{\"_key\":\"237feea872f9\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Impact: \"},{\"text\":\"Improve Atlas skills among local officials\\n\",\"_key\":\"c24a5a8362cc\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]},{\"text\":\"Geography: \",\"_key\":\"5faaf6a5961d\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"]},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Kenya\",\"_key\":\"1341ed0012bf\"}],\"_type\":\"block\"},{\"asset\":{\"_ref\":\"image-60c4d7b0cbbae74ec19b48777e3316b423a99e47-2048x1360-jpg\",\"_type\":\"reference\"},\"_type\":\"imageFull\",\"caption\":[{\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"764cd0a0a0ca\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"747a7891adbc\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Image Credit:\"},{\"text\":\" ©2010 CIAT/NeilPalmer\",\"_key\":\"30f43458ed0b\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}]}],\"_key\":\"94baf8bbaa20\"},{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Partners:\",\"_key\":\"823b1e160195\",\"_type\":\"span\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" Kenya County Governments\",\"_key\":\"f8a5db3f8a3f\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"bc24441d3d83\"}]},{\"title\":\"Analyzing greenhouse gas emissions in Uganda's cattle value chain to inform climate-smart livestock policies\",\"slug\":\"uganda-livestock-policy\",\"content\":[{\"_key\":\"948cb6b7cc93\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"text\":\"Synopsis\",\"_key\":\"fd7a8d0f5f46\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"]}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\"},{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Workshops in Bushenyi, Kasese and Kabarole with a total of 100+ participants yielded recommendations to integrate Atlas data into district climate planning. This helped shift the use case focus toward composting and biogas as a priority, while piloting less familiar options like biochar, BSF, and vermicomposting. Recognition of gender disparities prompted recommendations for gender-responsive training and greater inclusion of female extension staff. Extension officers identified additional training gaps, with inputs shaping future capacity-building plans. The evidence generated will support future proposals on livestock GHG mitigation, manure management infrastructure, and gender-responsive climate-smart agriculture.\\n\",\"_key\":\"456328ec466c\",\"_type\":\"span\"},{\"_key\":\"1d9f09266f67\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Stakeholder Group:\"},{\"_key\":\"2c78b52e8e26\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" Academia\\n\"},{\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Impact:\",\"_key\":\"4f3c8eb80906\",\"_type\":\"span\"},{\"text\":\" Measure GHGs\\n\",\"_key\":\"bb808ec84051\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Geography: \",\"_key\":\"00733a1b2dc6\"},{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Uganda\",\"_key\":\"3de6ff70b709\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"bec9759eded5\"},{\"asset\":{\"_type\":\"reference\",\"_ref\":\"image-33f2a6d99100994d9ee5374644daf82b152f6b9c-2048x1365-jpg\"},\"_type\":\"imageFull\",\"caption\":[{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Image Credit:\",\"_key\":\"1ce28f248638\",\"_type\":\"span\"},{\"text\":\" ©2016 CIAT/GeorginaSmith\",\"_key\":\"1e2f89188c57\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"122a2d909a07\"}],\"_key\":\"fd6921c57e0c\"},{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"ca900eed4e41\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Partners:\"},{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" Department of Agribusiness and Natural Resource Economics, Makerere University\",\"_key\":\"596857a0291e\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"2785e76f320a\"}],\"_id\":\"7bb5679e-a6de-4e0d-9476-039cf113e607\",\"_type\":\"impact\"},{\"_id\":\"7fe9a3fb-6fc1-4c75-92a8-78d50b1a7f85\",\"_type\":\"impact\",\"title\":\"Kenyan county governments access data on locally relevant adaptation strategies\",\"slug\":\"government-kenya\",\"content\":[{\"_key\":\"8e0aba743951\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Synopsis\",\"_key\":\"34ddc3a4f1c0\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\"},{\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"8834b592cc4b\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"c07cb1d78d36\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"The Adaptation Atlas, with its insights on the efficacy of on-farm practices under various conditions, equips local government authorities with the data needed to formulate evidence-based climate change response plans.\\n\\n\"},{\"text\":\"Use Case:\",\"_key\":\"9148f96265bb\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"]},{\"_key\":\"2452efbd20a6\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" Empowering local governance with actionable information on adaptation options for climate action\\n\"},{\"text\":\"Stakeholder Group:\",\"_key\":\"cd9e46ad7ace\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"]},{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" Government\\n\",\"_key\":\"233bb3497ef3\",\"_type\":\"span\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Impact:\",\"_key\":\"7c07da41988b\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" Shape policy\\n\",\"_key\":\"5d0f79056faa\"},{\"_key\":\"e5fa7986c838\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"KPI:\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" 3 plans influenced\\n\",\"_key\":\"efa5f3ca3c00\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Geography:\",\"_key\":\"8695c6f9cdd0\"},{\"_key\":\"4e1840187afc\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" Kenya\"}]},{\"_type\":\"imageFull\",\"alt\":\"Person in standing in a field of crops\",\"caption\":[{\"_key\":\"9da7ba7674c6\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"text\":\"Image credit:\",\"_key\":\"99de05efe144\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"]},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" ©2013CIAT/NathanRussell\",\"_key\":\"e76897151fb9\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\"}],\"_key\":\"a07cb078be8d\",\"asset\":{\"_type\":\"reference\",\"_ref\":\"image-25a6a49bc10643dbbc92cede4971f3b3b18c1a33-1560x1036-jpg\"}},{\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"865c777e1603\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"text\":\"Locally relevant data\",\"_key\":\"933846c2fb290\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}]},{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Counties across Kenya have been proactively developing strategies to make agriculture resilient to climate change. Local government authorities, in collaboration with multi-stakeholder platforms, have used insights from the Evidence for Resilient Agriculture (ERA) dataset, a portion of which is highlighted in the “On-farm Solutions for Today” spotlight. These strategic efforts were primarily aimed at dissecting and understanding the impacts of various management practices on crop yields and resilience across diverse Kenyan agroecosystems (i.e., agroecological zones).\",\"_key\":\"177bbf21a9a50\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"576d041d8174\"},{\"_key\":\"a1176b13fcd9\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"text\":\"By integrating these data, counties were able to craft tailored adaptation plans that were not only specific to their unique agricultural landscapes but also grounded in empirical evidence. These plans outlined actionable steps and interventions designed to enhance agricultural resilience, productivity, and sustainability. Furthermore, they consider the socio-economic dimensions of agricultural adaptation, ensuring that the proposed strategies are viable and beneficial for the local farming communities. The emphasis on local specificity and evidence-based decision-making marks a significant shift towards more informed and effective climate adaptation efforts at the county level.\",\"_key\":\"19026eff07500\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\"},{\"children\":[{\"text\":\"Partners\",\"_key\":\"40ae309afc8d0\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"2d57c9b45f2d\",\"markDefs\":[]},{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Kenyan Ministry of Agriculture, Livestock, Fisheries, and Irrigation, Climate Change Unit; governments of Nyeri, Taita-Taveta and Kajiado counties; FAO–Kenya; United States Department of Agriculture–Foreign Agricultural Service; International Center on Tropical Agriculture (CIAT).\",\"_key\":\"9b9b881124490\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"002b46a94b85\"}]},{\"_id\":\"c28657d3-a70d-4d72-b00a-750b78d277cf\",\"_type\":\"impact\",\"title\":\"Assessing the effectiveness of climate policy in mitigating low yields and crop losses among vulnerable households in Nigeria\",\"slug\":\"nigeria-mitigating-losses\",\"content\":[{\"_key\":\"f4b691d80b39\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Synopsis\",\"_key\":\"c881523edbd0\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\"},{\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"d14d76dd9109\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Following a workshop in Ibadan with 80+ participants, 7 research studies were completed using Atlas datasets. 14 more are in progress on PhD and MSc level, as well as in policy research. All studies reinforced alignment with Nigeria’s National Climate Change Policy (2021–2030) and National Agricultural Technology and Innovation Policy (2022–2027). In addition, this stimulated discussions with Nigerian research councils and international donors on climate-smart agriculture projects. Several institutions initiated step-down trainings at universities, extension services, and government agencies to further expand Atlas adoption.\",\"_key\":\"e215bf802151\"}],\"_type\":\"block\"},{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"\\n\",\"_key\":\"ace89aba0d8b\",\"_type\":\"span\"},{\"_key\":\"d9a3715cad33\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Stakeholder Group: \"},{\"_key\":\"f0da227097e0\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Research Organization, Governmental Agency, Academia\\n\"},{\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Impact: \",\"_key\":\"ab63ce2436e4\",\"_type\":\"span\"},{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Reinforce alignment with national climate change policies on agriculture and technology\\n\",\"_key\":\"0db28113e728\",\"_type\":\"span\"},{\"text\":\"Geography: \",\"_key\":\"c8c0865f4df5\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"]},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Nigeria\",\"_key\":\"41c4fbc32d2f\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"783b853f6e53\"},{\"_type\":\"imageFull\",\"caption\":[{\"_key\":\"c8f8ac1d7c93\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"c4a89fcccab9\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Image Credit: \"},{\"_key\":\"9c6aa9203001\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"©2023 CIAT/MiguelMamon\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\"}],\"_key\":\"54c1fa1835ba\",\"asset\":{\"_type\":\"reference\",\"_ref\":\"image-e806984b2adc6146a69f46dac3ce86492c46f240-2048x1365-jpg\"}},{\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"fd7d61f175b0\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Partners:\",\"_key\":\"7b90ee08fbe4\"},{\"_key\":\"13790b1befda\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" Innovation Lab for Policy Leadership in Agriculture and Food Security (PiLAF), University of Ibadan, Ministry of Agriculture and Food Security (Federal Level + Oyo State), Nigerian Stored Products Research Institute (NSPRI), Forestry Research Institute of Nigeria (FRIN), Cocoa Research Institute of Nigeria (CRIN), Nigerian Institute of Social and Economic Research (NISER), Institute of Agricultural Research and Training (IAR\\u0026T), National Horticultural Research Institute (NIHORT), National Centre for Genetic Resources and Biotechnology (NACGRAB), Universities and Colleges of Agriculture (University of Ibadan Departments + Federal Colleges)\"}],\"_type\":\"block\"}]},{\"title\":\"Evaluate Climate Risks\",\"featuredTags\":[{\"name\":\"Hazards\",\"slug\":{\"current\":\"hazards\",\"_type\":\"slug\"},\"_id\":\"d4f0b388-28d1-4707-86cb-3c89d9903357\"},{\"_id\":\"91d5bc42-a1ce-4f74-89c5-ef4c6489eb44\",\"name\":\"Exposure\",\"slug\":{\"_type\":\"slug\",\"current\":\"exposure\"}},{\"name\":\"Adaptive Capacity\",\"slug\":{\"_type\":\"slug\",\"current\":\"adaptive-capacity\"},\"_id\":\"f64dbad2-e40e-45f0-9318-8c8b46c3ef22\"}],\"_type\":\"spotlight\",\"_id\":\"3183ac0a-9746-4462-aefe-21ca004536bb\",\"content\":[{\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Overview\",\"_key\":\"d69a53f687c7\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"4e3885d9df45\",\"markDefs\":[]},{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"The 'Evaluate Climate Risks' Data Exploration supports stakeholders in making informed decisions for targeting adaptation and resilience-building initiatives based on the exposure of crop and livestock to climate hazards. Use this Observable Notebook data tool to:\",\"_key\":\"2bb5a467141d0\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"7b57e0dcb30b\"},{\"_key\":\"94329ecf329c\",\"listItem\":\"bullet\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Visualize the value of production and rural populations across Sub-saharan Africa down to country sub-regions\",\"_key\":\"4ca98bf839010\"}],\"level\":1,\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\"},{\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Compare the exposure of crops and livestock to climate hazards\",\"_key\":\"a6807d769c78\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"level\":1,\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"64fcd748e7a6\",\"listItem\":\"bullet\",\"markDefs\":[]},{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Identify vulnerable communities using three adaptive capacity metrics - education, female empowerment, and poverty - that indicate the adaptability of a population to the threats of climate change on critical agricultural systems\",\"_key\":\"e93708d0e68f\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"level\":1,\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"991958b8aaf5\",\"listItem\":\"bullet\"}],\"secondaryTags\":[{\"_id\":\"58596c78-8cbb-4f54-9a79-2c2b369f8f8c\",\"name\":\"Risk\"},{\"name\":\"Vulnerability\",\"_id\":\"cd9fa965-6b24-4995-b90e-4d91e3d1e9a4\"},{\"_id\":\"69c2847a-4d0e-4f02-8104-33190a8177e6\",\"name\":\"Value of Production\"},{\"_id\":\"8b90cad3-152c-4f0b-92e7-e4f866149664\",\"name\":\"Crops\"},{\"_id\":\"fd554b8b-784f-4fd9-8993-bd160474f28c\",\"name\":\"Livestock\"},{\"_id\":\"3aa7d3e8-8454-461c-86dc-349502040f33\",\"name\":\"Prioritization\"}],\"comingSoon\":false,\"slug\":\"evaluate-climate-risks\",\"primaryTags\":[{\"_id\":\"d4f0b388-28d1-4707-86cb-3c89d9903357\",\"name\":\"Hazards\",\"slug\":{\"current\":\"hazards\",\"_type\":\"slug\"}},{\"name\":\"Exposure\",\"slug\":{\"current\":\"exposure\",\"_type\":\"slug\"},\"_id\":\"91d5bc42-a1ce-4f74-89c5-ef4c6489eb44\"},{\"_id\":\"f64dbad2-e40e-45f0-9318-8c8b46c3ef22\",\"name\":\"Adaptive Capacity\",\"slug\":{\"current\":\"adaptive-capacity\",\"_type\":\"slug\"}}]},{\"primaryTags\":[{\"slug\":{\"current\":\"responses\",\"_type\":\"slug\"},\"_id\":\"1ca90184-e906-4102-bd9e-cac245b61a84\",\"name\":\"Responses\"},{\"_id\":\"e847ffae-f3a5-45fa-b8f2-ea7bbc82201e\",\"name\":\"Crops\",\"slug\":{\"_type\":\"slug\",\"current\":\"crops\"}},{\"name\":\"Implementation\",\"slug\":{\"current\":\"implementation\",\"_type\":\"slug\"},\"_id\":\"726273d7-9b34-4222-95e1-c796a793a590\"}],\"secondaryTags\":[{\"_id\":\"a4707273-18b4-4efb-bd4c-2f083bc33dc6\",\"name\":\"Management Practices\"},{\"name\":\"Benefits and Risks\",\"_id\":\"09c7b65b-de71-42e2-b4e2-ca10c7ced647\"},{\"_id\":\"4fc626b6-9a6e-4578-bbce-6ced34c170cf\",\"name\":\"Barriers to Adoption\"},{\"_id\":\"e0abe2d1-58d5-468e-a992-9058e3f3baa3\",\"name\":\"Agroecological Zones\"},{\"name\":\"Production\",\"_id\":\"c74bbffe-a437-437f-8dc6-eb3957627e0a\"},{\"name\":\"Yield\",\"_id\":\"3698a977-a654-40b6-8567-8d2c4d39de18\"}],\"_id\":\"1fe2aab8-12fb-4d99-815f-ed5d4f274d14\",\"_type\":\"spotlight\",\"title\":\"Discover Solutions\",\"slug\":\"discover-solutions\",\"content\":[{\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"95cc0b05a179\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"text\":\"Overview\",\"_key\":\"822063f6e9e8\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}],\"_type\":\"block\"},{\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"e5a3e3e2da43\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"This Data Exploration supports stakeholders in making informed decisions about viable adaptation practices and considerations for implementation. Use this Observable Notebook data tool to:\",\"_key\":\"dd44fe599488\",\"_type\":\"span\"}]},{\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"eb3192bcd2ad\",\"listItem\":\"bullet\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"See an at-a-glance view of the breadth of research across adaptation practices\",\"_key\":\"c1d538e7905a\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"level\":1,\"_type\":\"block\"},{\"listItem\":\"bullet\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Compare the range of practices used on specific crops, their average impact on crop yield, and the variability of practice impacts across different agroecological zones\",\"_key\":\"e30641510315\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"level\":1,\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"d6f8f15e5ae2\"},{\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"0fea0b5209ee\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Assess the risk of negative outcome for practices applied to crops alone or in combination with other practices\"}],\"level\":1,\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"10b913ba884b\",\"listItem\":\"bullet\",\"markDefs\":[]},{\"listItem\":\"bullet\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Learn which factors impact adoption\",\"_key\":\"061fdc3374e3\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"level\":1,\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"78b058403d7a\"},{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"text\":\"Access relevant guides to implement practices\",\"_key\":\"044a8bfee0dc\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}],\"level\":1,\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"06d6b4eb2535\",\"listItem\":\"bullet\"}],\"featuredTags\":[{\"_id\":\"1ca90184-e906-4102-bd9e-cac245b61a84\",\"name\":\"Responses\",\"slug\":{\"_type\":\"slug\",\"current\":\"responses\"}},{\"name\":\"Crops\",\"slug\":{\"current\":\"crops\",\"_type\":\"slug\"},\"_id\":\"e847ffae-f3a5-45fa-b8f2-ea7bbc82201e\"},{\"slug\":{\"_type\":\"slug\",\"current\":\"implementation\"},\"_id\":\"726273d7-9b34-4222-95e1-c796a793a590\",\"name\":\"Implementation\"}]},{\"_id\":\"a2f6e289-313f-4e71-8880-09b79a92e5f4\",\"_type\":\"spotlight\",\"title\":\"Analyze Women’s Exposure to Climate Hazards\",\"slug\":\"analyze-womens-exposure-to-climate-hazards\",\"content\":[{\"_key\":\"aa067f8c5c04\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"text\":\"Overview\",\"_key\":\"95243b69dc4b\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\"},{\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"d414ef2a61dd\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"This Data Exploration explores the intersection of agriculture, climate change, and gender. Use this Observable Notebook data tool to:\",\"_key\":\"5a0f92ffac950\"}]},{\"_key\":\"dedaec28793e\",\"listItem\":\"bullet\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"f0c28871b1a1\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Learn about the crops and agricultural practices in which women are most involved\"}],\"level\":1,\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\"},{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"670c423ce766\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Explore the different needs for gender-inclusive investments, in particular countries and regions\"}],\"level\":1,\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"ee79d36ee064\",\"listItem\":\"bullet\"},{\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"3821ce9656ac\",\"listItem\":\"bullet\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"See the geographic relationship between heat stress and the amount of women involved in agriculture today\",\"_key\":\"c0b2a44d300a\"}],\"level\":1}],\"featuredTags\":[{\"_id\":\"9f3a1112-4517-48c7-8466-f7871dbdea63\",\"name\":\"Gender\",\"slug\":{\"current\":\"gender\",\"_type\":\"slug\"}},{\"_id\":\"d4f0b388-28d1-4707-86cb-3c89d9903357\",\"name\":\"Hazards\",\"slug\":{\"current\":\"hazards\",\"_type\":\"slug\"}},{\"_id\":\"f64dbad2-e40e-45f0-9318-8c8b46c3ef22\",\"name\":\"Adaptive Capacity\",\"slug\":{\"current\":\"adaptive-capacity\",\"_type\":\"slug\"}}],\"primaryTags\":[{\"name\":\"Gender\",\"slug\":{\"current\":\"gender\",\"_type\":\"slug\"},\"_id\":\"9f3a1112-4517-48c7-8466-f7871dbdea63\"},{\"_id\":\"d4f0b388-28d1-4707-86cb-3c89d9903357\",\"name\":\"Hazards\",\"slug\":{\"current\":\"hazards\",\"_type\":\"slug\"}},{\"slug\":{\"current\":\"adaptive-capacity\",\"_type\":\"slug\"},\"_id\":\"f64dbad2-e40e-45f0-9318-8c8b46c3ef22\",\"name\":\"Adaptive Capacity\"}],\"secondaryTags\":[{\"_id\":\"18749454-95ee-49b2-a279-f92b7e731e9a\",\"name\":\"Women\"},{\"_id\":\"9a03a49d-22da-45d6-93e3-4026a60eab06\",\"name\":\"Hotspots\"},{\"_id\":\"cb7a184d-c626-47ec-b40a-d3c0f5bbb72b\",\"name\":\"Agency\"},{\"_id\":\"0b8f9564-acdf-4f98-8cd9-6e0288e24085\",\"name\":\"Empowerment\"}]},{\"featuredTags\":[{\"name\":\"Livestock\",\"slug\":{\"current\":\"livestock\",\"_type\":\"slug\"},\"_id\":\"6df6c598-0a3d-42c4-b7e9-5c4d459b3b7a\"},{\"slug\":{\"current\":\"investments\",\"_type\":\"slug\"},\"_id\":\"76c80111-f04f-4f08-bff3-f1504c86746f\",\"name\":\"Investments\"},{\"name\":\"Hazards\",\"slug\":{\"_type\":\"slug\",\"current\":\"hazards\"},\"_id\":\"d4f0b388-28d1-4707-86cb-3c89d9903357\"}],\"primaryTags\":[{\"slug\":{\"current\":\"livestock\",\"_type\":\"slug\"},\"_id\":\"6df6c598-0a3d-42c4-b7e9-5c4d459b3b7a\",\"name\":\"Livestock\"},{\"_id\":\"76c80111-f04f-4f08-bff3-f1504c86746f\",\"name\":\"Investments\",\"slug\":{\"current\":\"investments\",\"_type\":\"slug\"}},{\"_id\":\"d4f0b388-28d1-4707-86cb-3c89d9903357\",\"name\":\"Hazards\",\"slug\":{\"current\":\"hazards\",\"_type\":\"slug\"}}],\"secondaryTags\":[{\"_id\":\"363d9ba2-39f0-44d1-bf81-67f047a75d9d\",\"name\":\"Geography\"},{\"name\":\"Value of Production\",\"_id\":\"69c2847a-4d0e-4f02-8104-33190a8177e6\"},{\"_id\":\"74e9f33d-e623-4772-9334-87cf330044f7\",\"name\":\"Economics\"},{\"name\":\"Barriers to Adoption\",\"_id\":\"4fc626b6-9a6e-4578-bbce-6ced34c170cf\"},{\"name\":\"Adaptation\",\"_id\":\"e478041d-cefb-40cb-a57d-e12a62b49f3a\"},{\"_id\":\"03a000a2-7c85-4c30-99e7-0bdeba6d0685\",\"name\":\"Mitigation\"},{\"name\":\"Solutions\",\"_id\":\"28528d8c-94c6-4b48-8539-d773094bd83a\"},{\"name\":\"Responses\",\"_id\":\"ff37b304-06b1-426e-aa4d-cb1427344768\"}],\"_id\":\"8ee33480-3337-452e-89c8-e1259bb13d4e\",\"_type\":\"spotlight\",\"title\":\"Prioritize Livestock Investments\",\"slug\":\"prioritize-livestock-investments\",\"content\":[{\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Overview\",\"_key\":\"6a0a60eef5e2\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"b62180fbe361\",\"markDefs\":[]},{\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"b1a1a937b4b7\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"This Data Exploration focuses on livestock, a critical component of economic and food production systems in Africa. Because livestock are both at risk from climate change and a source of it, it is important to not only consider strategies for adaptation, but also mitigation. Use this Observable Notebook data tool to:\",\"_key\":\"562ee4abe44d0\",\"_type\":\"span\"}]},{\"level\":1,\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"b3cd49f15a26\",\"listItem\":\"bullet\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"text\":\"Explore the growth in different populations of livestock over time, along with their associated changes in Value of Production and Greenhouse Gas Emissions\",\"_key\":\"19878b38cb12\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}]},{\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"af8ff9114ea1\",\"listItem\":\"bullet\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"text\":\"See which countries would be most impactful to focus on given a particular weighting between adaptation and mitigation\",\"_key\":\"b926d705f04a\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}],\"level\":1},{\"level\":1,\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"b802822a1cfd\",\"listItem\":\"bullet\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Learn about specific, real-world solutions and the potential constraints to adopting them\",\"_key\":\"86220da95511\",\"_type\":\"span\"}]}]},{\"_id\":\"c8d356ea-a4c8-4e40-8544-e43f84c06749\",\"_type\":\"spotlight\",\"title\":\"Estimate Economic Returns on Adaptation\",\"slug\":\"estimate-economic-returns-on-adaptation\",\"content\":[{\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"c0790ed450fa\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"text\":\"Overview\",\"_key\":\"67e4a93166a90\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}]},{\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"f609f8975dfc\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"4a2d59e6072a0\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"The ‘Estimating Economic Returns on Adaptation’ Data Exploration helps users evaluate the potential benefits of an investment in an adaptation intervention. Use this Observable Notebook data tool to:\"}]},{\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"c1dbf67c0b18\",\"listItem\":\"bullet\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Explore the effects of parameters like the agricultural practice, the commodities to apply it on, the country to apply it in, and more\",\"_key\":\"aff5e74c037d\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"level\":1,\"_type\":\"block\"},{\"level\":1,\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"d1d9596e2f87\",\"listItem\":\"bullet\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Reveal the projected returns on an invested amount through key indicators like the Internal Rate of Return, Benefit-Cost Ratio, and Net Present Value\",\"_key\":\"f50b8cc84a74\",\"_type\":\"span\"}]}],\"featuredTags\":[{\"_id\":\"76c80111-f04f-4f08-bff3-f1504c86746f\",\"name\":\"Investments\",\"slug\":{\"_type\":\"slug\",\"current\":\"investments\"}},{\"slug\":{\"_type\":\"slug\",\"current\":\"prioritization\"},\"_id\":\"a2bb5681-640d-48d7-9619-252a4ad6a9a6\",\"name\":\"Prioritization\"},{\"name\":\"Implementation\",\"slug\":{\"current\":\"implementation\",\"_type\":\"slug\"},\"_id\":\"726273d7-9b34-4222-95e1-c796a793a590\"}],\"primaryTags\":[{\"_id\":\"76c80111-f04f-4f08-bff3-f1504c86746f\",\"name\":\"Investments\",\"slug\":{\"current\":\"investments\",\"_type\":\"slug\"}},{\"slug\":{\"_type\":\"slug\",\"current\":\"prioritization\"},\"_id\":\"a2bb5681-640d-48d7-9619-252a4ad6a9a6\",\"name\":\"Prioritization\"},{\"slug\":{\"current\":\"implementation\",\"_type\":\"slug\"},\"_id\":\"726273d7-9b34-4222-95e1-c796a793a590\",\"name\":\"Implementation\"}],\"secondaryTags\":[{\"name\":\"Economics\",\"_id\":\"74e9f33d-e623-4772-9334-87cf330044f7\"},{\"_id\":\"80032f35-e371-48c7-b10f-1ff74b322e68\",\"name\":\"Finance\"},{\"_id\":\"f722d529-a26c-4406-b602-02bcf94fe403\",\"name\":\"Return on Investment\"},{\"_id\":\"363d9ba2-39f0-44d1-bf81-67f047a75d9d\",\"name\":\"Geography\"},{\"name\":\"Crops\",\"_id\":\"8b90cad3-152c-4f0b-92e7-e4f866149664\"},{\"_id\":\"fd554b8b-784f-4fd9-8993-bd160474f28c\",\"name\":\"Livestock\"}]},{\"slug\":\"feeling-the-heat\",\"content\":[{\"_key\":\"dcb26850118a\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Introduction\",\"_key\":\"670b839511f90\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\"},{\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Heat is a multi-faceted problem for agriculture. It affects the agricultural sector through a variety of mechanisms, differing in time and place.\",\"_key\":\"1a21fde8cd400\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"40884becaa0d\",\"markDefs\":[]},{\"_type\":\"imageFull\",\"alt\":\"Data Insight, Featured Image: Feeling the heat\",\"_key\":\"e4eb896cb6d7\",\"asset\":{\"_type\":\"reference\",\"_ref\":\"image-6398ed204826239fb028227e689af5c22f98810b-1560x1036-jpg\"}},{\"_key\":\"bf3b4e989f44\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"500 million people live in rural areas suffering from heat stress\",\"_key\":\"42e1b5b967d90\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\"},{\"_key\":\"e58e478c1d3f\",\"markDefs\":[{\"_key\":\"26d4cd45b4de\",\"_type\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://www.science.org/doi/10.1126/sciadv.aaw1838\"},{\"_type\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0160412018328654?via%3Dihub\",\"_key\":\"d52d36a829b0\"},{\"_key\":\"b096aff1980b\",\"_type\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://iopscience.iop.org/article/10.1088/1748-9326/ab86f4\"}],\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"6bbfbe04bbe60\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"There is now an abundance of evidence that heat has effects on people (\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"26d4cd45b4de\"],\"text\":\"Raymond et al., 2020\",\"_key\":\"a8384c634496\"},{\"_key\":\"4e2006f42ada\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"; \"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"d52d36a829b0\"],\"text\":\"Sun et al., 2019\",\"_key\":\"1d0e6625205f\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"; \",\"_key\":\"e7fe5d7f6dd4\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"b096aff1980b\"],\"text\":\"Tigchelaar et al., 2020\",\"_key\":\"6d147ba7570c\"},{\"_key\":\"9f13963107fb\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"). Heat stress occurs when the heat received by the body is greater than the body can tolerate. This causes physiological impairment, which can lead to heat stroke and, in extreme cases, death. It affects the health of farm workers directly, reducing labor productivity which, in turn, has an impact on the income generated by farms. We define heat stress on people as occurring when daytime temperatures exceed 32°C. We find that over 500 million people live in rural areas suffering from heat stress at some point during the year, with the greatest concentration in the Sahel.\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\"},{\"_type\":\"imageCaption\",\"alt\":\"Data Insight 1, Map 1: Combined effects of heat on people, crops and livestock (cattle)\",\"caption\":[{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"e56d99e559d60\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Map 1\"},{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" Combined effects of heat on people, crops and livestock (cattle). It shows the areas where multiple heat-related hazards coincide, using projected temperature data for 2030\",\"_key\":\"4d218d355a78\",\"_type\":\"span\"},{\"text\":\"1\",\"_key\":\"130288c72692\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"super\"]},{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\".\",\"_key\":\"f1a35ac6c000\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"ed0b18a019e9\"}],\"_key\":\"a4a49ef059f8\",\"asset\":{\"_ref\":\"image-4d92aad6628d0ebbaaaa275b2d426dc816abe7c1-1920x1129-png\",\"_type\":\"reference\"}},{\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"2ea926641c69\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Around 46 million hectares of crops are projected to be heat stressed in 2030\",\"_key\":\"942dfe7695bd0\"}]},{\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"6dba15155608\",\"markDefs\":[{\"_type\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://iopscience.iop.org/article/10.1088/1748-9326/8/2/024041\",\"_key\":\"1eb25e65317b\"},{\"_key\":\"22cdafc429fe\",\"_type\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S1470160X15002058?via%3Dihub\"},{\"_type\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0168192311002784?via%3Dihub\",\"_key\":\"1ef218dc272d\"}],\"children\":[{\"text\":\"Heat also affects crops at a range of physiological stages (from early growth through to flowering and seeding/fruiting) and different times of the day (with nighttime temperatures affecting crops just as much as those in daytime). The effect varies depending on the crop and variety, with heat-tolerant species such as sorghum and cassava being much less affected than heat-sensitive ones such as beans, wheat, maize or potato (\",\"_key\":\"1cd90e7a75250\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]},{\"text\":\"Gourdji et al., 2013\",\"_key\":\"8a5dc0a198dd\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"1eb25e65317b\"]},{\"text\":\"; \",\"_key\":\"5a70c3c04ae7\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"22cdafc429fe\"],\"text\":\"Siebert and Ewert, 2014\",\"_key\":\"fa5b71783658\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"; \",\"_key\":\"d0528c106a46\"},{\"_key\":\"a1f57e1c0a50\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"1ef218dc272d\"],\"text\":\"Teixeira et al., 2013\"},{\"_key\":\"752f4c3ffce4\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\").\"}]},{\"children\":[{\"text\":\"We calculated the effect of heat stress on a range of crops by calculating the number of days above a crop-specific temperature threshold per month, with more than five days of excess heat signifying moderate-to-high heat stress. Around 46 million hectares of crops are projected to be heat stressed in 2030, with the greatest effects in the northern Sahel\",\"_key\":\"dbff62a39f360\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"super\"],\"text\":\"2\",\"_key\":\"a53b622afe8f\"},{\"_key\":\"31c14814fa3a\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\".\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"9e36e55d6d96\",\"markDefs\":[]},{\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"809 million hectares have moderate-to-high heat stress, accounting for 116 million head of cattle\",\"_key\":\"008b6e5ebbd9\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"0cb08d3e65a7\",\"markDefs\":[]},{\"markDefs\":[{\"_key\":\"7e40e7fdeb26\",\"_type\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S221209631730027X?via%3Dihub\"}],\"children\":[{\"text\":\"Finally, heat affects livestock. When ambient temperatures, humidity and radiant energy soar, animals are impaired in multiple ways. Initially, heat stress causes animals to divert energy away from producing meat, milk or other products to maintaining homeostasis. Progressively higher heat stress affects behaviour and causes metabolic variations, which impacts animal health and may cause mortality (\",\"_key\":\"ace15a4a45a10\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]},{\"_key\":\"167253cdaecc\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"7e40e7fdeb26\"],\"text\":\"Rojas-Downing et al., 2017\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\").\",\"_key\":\"4f255e89dfd2\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"c8a97bc393bb\"},{\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"588f4f8b4d14\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"As with crops, some livestock species and breeds are more resistant than others. We calculated the heat stress on livestock using the temperature-humidity index, classifying moderate-to-high heat stress as occurring with scores over 78. Results show that heat stress is a problem across many livestock-producing regions of sub-Saharan Africa (SSA), from southern Africa to the Sahel. A total of 809 million hectares have moderate-to-high heat stress, accounting for 116 million head of cattle worth $92.8 billion International Dollars today.\",\"_key\":\"c8f3637ad4d50\"}],\"_type\":\"block\"},{\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"99454e4d0f2d\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"When heat stress simultaneously affects people, crops and livestock, the livelihoods and health of farmers and their families are at risk\",\"_key\":\"56b5244af0df0\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"_type\":\"block\"},{\"caption\":[{\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"1063c0b4be50\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"4b97d2124f4c0\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Map 2 (left)\"},{\"_key\":\"b0c1a3370eb5\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" Heat stress in crops in 2030, \"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Map 3 (center)\",\"_key\":\"f56d396f78b3\"},{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" Heat stress in people in 2030, \",\"_key\":\"aedc6e3b4a38\",\"_type\":\"span\"},{\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Map 4 (right)\",\"_key\":\"bae79f4c5a93\",\"_type\":\"span\"},{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" Heat stress in livestock 2030.\",\"_key\":\"ad114695e1a6\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"_type\":\"block\"}],\"_key\":\"ed094278a96e\",\"asset\":{\"_ref\":\"image-6b75cf0a9b21090f711b8bd33709e4a9e4b6ded4-1920x618-png\",\"_type\":\"reference\"},\"_type\":\"imageCaption\",\"alt\":\"Data Insight 1, Maps 2, 3, 4: Heat stress in crops, people and livestock in 2030 \"},{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"When heat stress simultaneously affects people, crops and livestock, the livelihoods and health of farmers and their families are at risk. In many areas of the Sahel, heat stress occurs around springtime, impairing livestock production and affecting farmers’ health and ability to prepare the land. Later in the year (towards August), heat stress affects crops, reducing food availability and farmers’ capacity to harvest.\",\"_key\":\"73b2fd4e6fa60\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"5a115af21729\"},{\"_key\":\"ac13de4bbe3b\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Heat-stressed crops require greater upkeep by farmers, while at the same time livestock need continued supplies of feed (from crops). Thus, the effects of heat stress interact with each other, creating significant challenges to maintaining agricultural livelihoods.\",\"_key\":\"11a0ff3f05000\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\"},{\"_key\":\"d500318f8534\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"45 million hectares of crops worth $18.4 billion International Dollars will be located in areas of high heat stress in people, crops and livestock\",\"_key\":\"21090fafd95d\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\"},{\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"By 2030, we found that 45 million hectares of crops worth $18.4 billion International Dollars will be located in areas of high heat stress in people, crops and livestock, with 51 million smallholder farmers affected\",\"_key\":\"6f50661e4487\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"super\"],\"text\":\"3\",\"_key\":\"49b609907dbc\"},{\"_key\":\"053c63e1a2da\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\". For these areas, a range of adaptation options must be promoted, including heat-resistant crop varieties and livestock breeds, shade-based production systems to reduce field temperatures, and mechanization to reduce drudgery and the risks of heat stress to human health.\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"80640c7b4af6\",\"markDefs\":[]}],\"_id\":\"67001a4c-586f-4812-b6d2-81682b1615f3\",\"_type\":\"insight\",\"title\":\"Feeling the heat – the effects of higher temperatures on people, crops and livestock\"},{\"secondaryTags\":[{\"_id\":\"363d9ba2-39f0-44d1-bf81-67f047a75d9d\",\"name\":\"Geography\"},{\"_id\":\"c01c093b-fb00-4c23-9adb-ba1c651d54c0\",\"name\":\"Harvest\"},{\"name\":\"Structural Change\",\"_id\":\"77a729cf-515c-44ae-a6fb-a931e93dd49a\"},{\"_id\":\"3d733224-ae5d-4f3c-b5f2-e2dccf737b89\",\"name\":\"Climate Justice\"},{\"_id\":\"e478041d-cefb-40cb-a57d-e12a62b49f3a\",\"name\":\"Adaptation\"}],\"_id\":\"a9ca87b1-d1ec-48e4-a942-b1b5abf31c2e\",\"_type\":\"spotlight\",\"title\":\"Understand Heat Stress on Producers\",\"slug\":\"understand-heat-stress-on-producers\",\"content\":[{\"_key\":\"7444a0e25f73\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Overview\",\"_key\":\"700b014f247d0\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\"},{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"The ‘Understand Heat Stress on Producers’ Data Exploration provides critical data to make informed decisions for targeting geographically explicit adaptation for the agricultural workforce. Use this Observable Notebook data tool to:\",\"_key\":\"2b4d64393314\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"b3cfea896cd2\"},{\"level\":1,\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"e0aa4ef255ed\",\"listItem\":\"bullet\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"text\":\"Visualize the size of the African agricultural workforce today and in the future based on projected economic and social development trajectories\",\"_key\":\"de6cb282dfc80\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}]},{\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"b81a8eea5023\",\"listItem\":\"bullet\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"text\":\"Identify the heat stress exposure to different geographies under different climate projections against a baseline\",\"_key\":\"c3803ae864560\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}],\"level\":1,\"_type\":\"block\"},{\"level\":1,\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"461530134fb4\",\"listItem\":\"bullet\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"6cf4c46f530c0\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Assess the proportion of the hours during growing season that will surpass safe working conditions for different populations\"}]}],\"featuredTags\":[{\"_id\":\"13341a00-ef64-4067-9b65-c517a4dc3685\",\"name\":\"Labour\",\"slug\":{\"_type\":\"slug\",\"current\":\"labour\"}},{\"_id\":\"b75173e9-b0e6-48d1-bba3-262b47471729\",\"name\":\"Heat Stress\",\"slug\":{\"_type\":\"slug\",\"current\":\"heat-stress\"}},{\"slug\":{\"current\":\"projections\",\"_type\":\"slug\"},\"_id\":\"9b08ebf8-9f22-46de-9224-883253b72281\",\"name\":\"Projections\"}],\"primaryTags\":[{\"_id\":\"13341a00-ef64-4067-9b65-c517a4dc3685\",\"name\":\"Labour\",\"slug\":{\"current\":\"labour\",\"_type\":\"slug\"}},{\"slug\":{\"current\":\"heat-stress\",\"_type\":\"slug\"},\"_id\":\"b75173e9-b0e6-48d1-bba3-262b47471729\",\"name\":\"Heat Stress\"},{\"_id\":\"9b08ebf8-9f22-46de-9224-883253b72281\",\"name\":\"Projections\",\"slug\":{\"current\":\"projections\",\"_type\":\"slug\"}}]},{\"featuredTags\":[{\"slug\":{\"_type\":\"slug\",\"current\":\"crops\"},\"_id\":\"e847ffae-f3a5-45fa-b8f2-ea7bbc82201e\",\"name\":\"Crops\"},{\"_id\":\"7262fa5c-469d-4e64-bcf1-a1300e7092bb\",\"name\":\"Impacts\",\"slug\":{\"current\":\"impacts\",\"_type\":\"slug\"}},{\"_id\":\"1ca90184-e906-4102-bd9e-cac245b61a84\",\"name\":\"Responses\",\"slug\":{\"current\":\"responses\",\"_type\":\"slug\"}}],\"slug\":\"view-projected-climate-impacts\",\"_type\":\"spotlight\",\"comingSoon\":false,\"secondaryTags\":[{\"name\":\"Crop Models\",\"_id\":\"09ca31f7-e015-4524-b0c8-78950a53c60f\"},{\"_id\":\"28528d8c-94c6-4b48-8539-d773094bd83a\",\"name\":\"Solutions\"},{\"name\":\"Cereals\",\"_id\":\"3836a8f6-a22b-4feb-9372-e8a60d412d86\"},{\"_id\":\"11db2902-45d9-4632-a2f5-1c8d20f7e93c\",\"name\":\"Varieties\"},{\"_id\":\"f72e184e-496e-4dfe-b8c2-06f1fa6277ae\",\"name\":\"Cultivars\"},{\"_id\":\"adc7a222-0f41-4078-b476-4c20ec28c2c7\",\"name\":\"Irrigation\"},{\"_id\":\"ba08f63c-c52d-4830-a980-f6679fe04927\",\"name\":\"Adaptation Options\"}],\"title\":\"View Projected Climate Impacts \",\"content\":[{\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Overview\",\"_key\":\"bfe850eee494\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"dcc6b51d7c19\",\"markDefs\":[]},{\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"f95e394052d4\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Cereal grains provide 50% of the daily caloric intake in sub-Saharan Africa. By 2050, the population of this region will more than double, and they will need to grow food on the same amount of arable land. Adaptation is crucial to evade the dire consequences of climate change on this increasingly important food supply. Use this Observable Notebook data tool to:\",\"_key\":\"85f14db48ee0\"}],\"_type\":\"block\"},{\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"dbbd83402bfc0\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Explore the impact of climate change on key crops in sub-Saharan Africa compared to other parts of the world\"}],\"level\":1,\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"d0878571ba27\",\"listItem\":\"bullet\",\"markDefs\":[]},{\"children\":[{\"text\":\"Analyze specific projected changes to crops within particular sub-Saharan African countries and regions within them\",\"_key\":\"d28fea6f45dd0\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}],\"level\":1,\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"0448aae3b212\",\"listItem\":\"bullet\",\"markDefs\":[]},{\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"d510591af73c\",\"listItem\":\"bullet\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Learn to what degree specific adaptation solutions can mitigate these changes\",\"_key\":\"25583f51ce430\"}],\"level\":1}],\"_id\":\"78b36032-2778-40a5-8b9c-6f1a47ed84a1\",\"primaryTags\":[{\"_id\":\"e847ffae-f3a5-45fa-b8f2-ea7bbc82201e\",\"name\":\"Crops\",\"slug\":{\"_type\":\"slug\",\"current\":\"crops\"}},{\"_id\":\"7262fa5c-469d-4e64-bcf1-a1300e7092bb\",\"name\":\"Impacts\",\"slug\":{\"current\":\"impacts\",\"_type\":\"slug\"}},{\"_id\":\"1ca90184-e906-4102-bd9e-cac245b61a84\",\"name\":\"Responses\",\"slug\":{\"current\":\"responses\",\"_type\":\"slug\"}}]},{\"secondaryTags\":[{\"name\":\"Projections\",\"_id\":\"de303226-0374-4fde-aed7-b048d94a834a\"},{\"name\":\"Gender\",\"_id\":\"a57b36dc-353a-41d0-ad5b-cf607342171b\"},{\"name\":\"Climate\",\"_id\":\"22aeb3c6-8d4a-469d-a763-2122741616b6\"},{\"_id\":\"58596c78-8cbb-4f54-9a79-2c2b369f8f8c\",\"name\":\"Risk\"},{\"name\":\"Vulnerability\",\"_id\":\"cd9fa965-6b24-4995-b90e-4d91e3d1e9a4\"},{\"_id\":\"363d9ba2-39f0-44d1-bf81-67f047a75d9d\",\"name\":\"Geography\"}],\"primaryTags\":[{\"slug\":{\"_type\":\"slug\",\"current\":\"hazards\"},\"_id\":\"d4f0b388-28d1-4707-86cb-3c89d9903357\",\"name\":\"Hazards\"},{\"_id\":\"91d5bc42-a1ce-4f74-89c5-ef4c6489eb44\",\"name\":\"Exposure\",\"slug\":{\"current\":\"exposure\",\"_type\":\"slug\"}},{\"_id\":\"f64dbad2-e40e-45f0-9318-8c8b46c3ef22\",\"name\":\"Adaptive Capacity\",\"slug\":{\"current\":\"adaptive-capacity\",\"_type\":\"slug\"}}],\"_id\":\"7347a7a8-af1f-4161-94c0-45de2f563858\",\"featuredTags\":[{\"_id\":\"d4f0b388-28d1-4707-86cb-3c89d9903357\",\"name\":\"Hazards\",\"slug\":{\"_type\":\"slug\",\"current\":\"hazards\"}},{\"slug\":{\"current\":\"exposure\",\"_type\":\"slug\"},\"_id\":\"91d5bc42-a1ce-4f74-89c5-ef4c6489eb44\",\"name\":\"Exposure\"},{\"_id\":\"f64dbad2-e40e-45f0-9318-8c8b46c3ef22\",\"name\":\"Adaptive Capacity\",\"slug\":{\"current\":\"adaptive-capacity\",\"_type\":\"slug\"}}],\"content\":[{\"children\":[{\"text\":\"This data exploration tool enables exploration and download of the data that underpins the Africa Agricultural Adaptation Atlas. The tool provides a platform for stakeholders to visualize and download data for their own analysis and insights. The tool can be used to discover patterns between datasets, countries, and regions. Use this Observable Notebook to:\",\"_key\":\"29357ecc3ea40\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"dc3595b63fe9\",\"markDefs\":[]},{\"_key\":\"7734379104d3\",\"listItem\":\"bullet\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Gain in-depth insights into climate risk variables using the integrated table and plot tools.\",\"_key\":\"9b1c0f8b12aa0\"}],\"level\":1,\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\"},{\"level\":1,\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"10573a5395f9\",\"listItem\":\"bullet\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Filter and export data across variables and regions of interest for external analysis in multiple formats.\",\"_key\":\"0a8f0e18535b0\"}]},{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"text\":\"Visualize data to uncover valuable insights into spatial patterns of climate risk within and between countries.\",\"_key\":\"5b818bf2c1010\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}],\"level\":1,\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"9956f7f3cfde\",\"listItem\":\"bullet\"},{\"level\":1,\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"465d819fa97c\",\"listItem\":\"bullet\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Learn how to access our Spatio Temporal Asset Catalog STAC catalog to access the raw data.\",\"_key\":\"f73173f1c4ee0\"}]}],\"title\":\"Explore the Datasets\",\"comingSoon\":false,\"prototype\":false,\"_type\":\"spotlight\",\"slug\":\"explore-the-datasets\"},{\"primaryTags\":[{\"slug\":{\"current\":\"investments\",\"_type\":\"slug\"},\"_id\":\"76c80111-f04f-4f08-bff3-f1504c86746f\",\"name\":\"Investments\"},{\"name\":\"Hazards\",\"slug\":{\"_type\":\"slug\",\"current\":\"hazards\"},\"_id\":\"d4f0b388-28d1-4707-86cb-3c89d9903357\"},{\"_id\":\"9e65ed0e-dc8c-4778-8f9a-d487428621a3\",\"name\":\"Solutions\",\"slug\":{\"current\":\"solutions\",\"_type\":\"slug\"}}],\"comingSoon\":false,\"slug\":\"formulate-a-climate-rationale-for-projects\",\"underMaintenance\":false,\"secondaryTags\":[{\"_id\":\"de303226-0374-4fde-aed7-b048d94a834a\",\"name\":\"Projections\"},{\"_id\":\"31f649ae-7bc4-4e71-892f-fb8839fd8125\",\"name\":\"Exposure\"},{\"_id\":\"b9c8e441-7bf5-4867-83a4-7a4869ffb356\",\"name\":\"Adaptive Capacity\"},{\"_id\":\"3aa7d3e8-8454-461c-86dc-349502040f33\",\"name\":\"Prioritization\"},{\"_id\":\"1782ff10-e41b-422c-bf00-cad9f88dd026\",\"name\":\"Climate Rationale\"},{\"name\":\"Investments\",\"_id\":\"7031a744-6f2e-4ff5-987a-0cafb94e95b7\"}],\"_id\":\"384610e2-52f3-4c45-a42e-afb48064e345\",\"title\":\"Formulate a Climate Rationale for Projects\",\"featuredTags\":[{\"_id\":\"76c80111-f04f-4f08-bff3-f1504c86746f\",\"name\":\"Investments\",\"slug\":{\"current\":\"investments\",\"_type\":\"slug\"}},{\"slug\":{\"current\":\"hazards\",\"_type\":\"slug\"},\"_id\":\"d4f0b388-28d1-4707-86cb-3c89d9903357\",\"name\":\"Hazards\"},{\"name\":\"Solutions\",\"slug\":{\"current\":\"solutions\",\"_type\":\"slug\"},\"_id\":\"9e65ed0e-dc8c-4778-8f9a-d487428621a3\"}],\"_type\":\"spotlight\",\"content\":[{\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"01348ccda3de\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"text\":\"This data exploration tool supports stakeholders in developing a robust climate rationale, providing an evidence base to understanding the climate risks and selecting related solutions for a project or investment. The tool presents critical data points that illustrate the extent and impact of climate change on specific crops, livestock, and geographic regions, alongside possible response strategies. Use this Observable Notebook to:\",\"_key\":\"248088bc62fd0\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}]},{\"listItem\":\"bullet\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"7310a16555d00\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Access demographic and economic information for individual countries.\"}],\"level\":1,\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"0dc782d1415a\"},{\"level\":1,\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"9a96e77e7419\",\"listItem\":\"bullet\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"text\":\"Analyze recent trends in key climate indicators, such as mean temperature.\",\"_key\":\"dae368dac222\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}]},{\"listItem\":\"bullet\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Explore future climate projections under various scenarios of climate change severity.\",\"_key\":\"c718a12493e8\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"level\":1,\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"735fd029133a\"},{\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"13e99a3db238\",\"listItem\":\"bullet\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"text\":\"Assess the vulnerability of specific crop and livestock groups to climate impacts.\",\"_key\":\"2fb6da784579\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}],\"level\":1,\"_type\":\"block\"},{\"_key\":\"ceb939cfb0f1\",\"listItem\":\"bullet\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Identify potential solutions to mitigate climate risks and enhance resilience.\\n\",\"_key\":\"9f58422bf30a\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"level\":1,\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\"},{\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"d755fe010f9f\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"text\":\"This data exploration is a beta version and will be updated with additional data, features, and functionality.\",\"_key\":\"09e109d90617\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"em\"]}],\"_type\":\"block\"}]},{\"title\":\"Identify Vulnerability\",\"prototype\":false,\"primaryTags\":[{\"_id\":\"f64dbad2-e40e-45f0-9318-8c8b46c3ef22\",\"name\":\"Adaptive Capacity\",\"slug\":{\"current\":\"adaptive-capacity\",\"_type\":\"slug\"}},{\"slug\":{\"current\":\"hazards\",\"_type\":\"slug\"},\"_id\":\"d4f0b388-28d1-4707-86cb-3c89d9903357\",\"name\":\"Hazards\"},{\"name\":\"Gender\",\"slug\":{\"current\":\"gender\",\"_type\":\"slug\"},\"_id\":\"9f3a1112-4517-48c7-8466-f7871dbdea63\"}],\"content\":[{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"This notebook integrates dimensions of urgency and adaptive capacity into a composite vulnerability index. The notebook combines indicators such as population density, crop exposure to climate hazards, poverty, education, and multiple adaptive capacity variables to identify areas where risks \\u0026 population sensitivity are high and the ability to respond is limited.\",\"_key\":\"fce10ea229c3\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"6ad56389e53d\"},{\"_key\":\"bb7e86582146\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"text\":\"The notebook also includes gender-disaggregated sensitivity analysis, examining how poverty and education intersect for men and women within specific regions. It highlights the share of populations experiencing overlapping disadvantages, such as high poverty and low education.\",\"_key\":\"c81c61dac3ff\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\"}],\"_id\":\"9952fab5-350c-4f14-bef9-8603d56a7626\",\"slug\":\"identify-vulnerability\",\"_type\":\"spotlight\",\"comingSoon\":false,\"featuredTags\":[{\"name\":\"Adaptive Capacity\",\"slug\":{\"_type\":\"slug\",\"current\":\"adaptive-capacity\"},\"_id\":\"f64dbad2-e40e-45f0-9318-8c8b46c3ef22\"},{\"name\":\"Hazards\",\"slug\":{\"current\":\"hazards\",\"_type\":\"slug\"},\"_id\":\"d4f0b388-28d1-4707-86cb-3c89d9903357\"},{\"_id\":\"9f3a1112-4517-48c7-8466-f7871dbdea63\",\"name\":\"Gender\",\"slug\":{\"current\":\"gender\",\"_type\":\"slug\"}}]},{\"slug\":\"cis-readiness\",\"content\":[{\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"3b9f85737658\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Reliable Climate Information Services (CIS) depend on a continuous chain of functions: observation, data agreement, prediction and usability. This notebook helps users identify where climate information is reliable enough to inform agricultural decisions and where weak data infrastructure could limit impact.\",\"_key\":\"45e20b6ab771\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"_type\":\"block\"}],\"featuredTags\":[{\"slug\":{\"_type\":\"slug\",\"current\":\"hazards\"},\"_id\":\"d4f0b388-28d1-4707-86cb-3c89d9903357\",\"name\":\"Hazards\"},{\"slug\":{\"_type\":\"slug\",\"current\":\"prioritization\"},\"_id\":\"a2bb5681-640d-48d7-9619-252a4ad6a9a6\",\"name\":\"Prioritization\"}],\"_id\":\"446d22b3-8e3e-4560-9836-b9e6f9230781\",\"_type\":\"spotlight\",\"title\":\"Climate Information Readiness\",\"prototype\":false},{\"prototype\":true,\"slug\":\"climate-rationale-v2\",\"title\":\"Climate Rationale V2\",\"underMaintenance\":false,\"_id\":\"41166743-361d-4476-8c2b-7bf31bd61377\",\"featuredTags\":[{\"_id\":\"76c80111-f04f-4f08-bff3-f1504c86746f\",\"name\":\"Investments\",\"slug\":{\"current\":\"investments\",\"_type\":\"slug\"}},{\"name\":\"Hazards\",\"slug\":{\"_type\":\"slug\",\"current\":\"hazards\"},\"_id\":\"d4f0b388-28d1-4707-86cb-3c89d9903357\"},{\"_id\":\"9e65ed0e-dc8c-4778-8f9a-d487428621a3\",\"name\":\"Solutions\",\"slug\":{\"current\":\"solutions\",\"_type\":\"slug\"}}],\"secondaryTags\":[{\"name\":\"Projections\",\"_id\":\"de303226-0374-4fde-aed7-b048d94a834a\"},{\"_id\":\"31f649ae-7bc4-4e71-892f-fb8839fd8125\",\"name\":\"Exposure\"},{\"name\":\"Adaptive Capacity\",\"_id\":\"b9c8e441-7bf5-4867-83a4-7a4869ffb356\"},{\"_id\":\"3aa7d3e8-8454-461c-86dc-349502040f33\",\"name\":\"Prioritization\"},{\"_id\":\"1782ff10-e41b-422c-bf00-cad9f88dd026\",\"name\":\"Climate Rationale\"},{\"_id\":\"7031a744-6f2e-4ff5-987a-0cafb94e95b7\",\"name\":\"Investments\"}],\"_type\":\"spotlight\",\"comingSoon\":false,\"content\":[{\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"9e89be94b973\",\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"text\":\"This data exploration tool supports stakeholders in developing a robust climate rationale, providing an evidence base to understanding the climate risks and selecting related solutions for a project or investment. The tool presents critical data points that illustrate the extent and impact of climate change on specific crops, livestock, and geographic regions, alongside possible response strategies. Use this Observable Notebook to:\",\"_key\":\"9aea3543acc0\"}]},{\"listItem\":\"bullet\",\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"b3179afbe1f0\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"text\":\"Access demographic and economic information for individual countries.\"}],\"level\":1,\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"3aaccd3b0999\"},{\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"text\":\"Analyze recent trends in key climate indicators, such as mean temperature.\",\"_key\":\"64b12dae0d0b\"}],\"level\":1,\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"a7410b53e947\",\"listItem\":\"bullet\"},{\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"text\":\"Explore future climate projections under various scenarios of climate change severity.\",\"_key\":\"7b5732f3b294\"}],\"level\":1,\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"e3ecee919492\",\"listItem\":\"bullet\"},{\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"974e1b78473e\",\"listItem\":\"bullet\",\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"67ef1775d5c8\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"text\":\"Assess the vulnerability of specific crop and livestock groups to climate impacts.\"}],\"level\":1,\"_type\":\"block\"},{\"_key\":\"921d37fbf0d1\",\"listItem\":\"bullet\",\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"text\":\"Identify potential solutions to mitigate climate risks and enhance resilience.\\n\",\"_key\":\"5b38b8154bd6\"}],\"level\":1,\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\"},{\"children\":[{\"text\":\"This data exploration is a beta version and will be updated with additional data, features, and functionality.\",\"_key\":\"f498262de20c\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"em\"]}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"1ad99d18bd1f\"}],\"primaryTags\":[{\"_id\":\"76c80111-f04f-4f08-bff3-f1504c86746f\",\"name\":\"Investments\",\"slug\":{\"_type\":\"slug\",\"current\":\"investments\"}},{\"name\":\"Hazards\",\"slug\":{\"current\":\"hazards\",\"_type\":\"slug\"},\"_id\":\"d4f0b388-28d1-4707-86cb-3c89d9903357\"},{\"_id\":\"9e65ed0e-dc8c-4778-8f9a-d487428621a3\",\"name\":\"Solutions\",\"slug\":{\"current\":\"solutions\",\"_type\":\"slug\"}}]},{\"_id\":\"43874bd9-d7e1-4554-bb04-7287fea7aa74\",\"_type\":\"impact\",\"title\":\"The World Bank assessed the viability of adaptation investments with a model integrated into the Atlas\",\"slug\":\"world-bank-aiccra\",\"content\":[{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"text\":\"Synopsis\",\"_key\":\"12916dc27ff2\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"5caf2af224d0\"},{\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"6cae332d7cba\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"The Atlas' economic return model, developed during conception of the AICCRA program, generates key economic performance indicators to support investor decisions.\\n\\n\",\"_key\":\"bd164e330b0f0\",\"_type\":\"span\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Use Case:\",\"_key\":\"67cca4e5c503\"},{\"_key\":\"0b7a62334d78\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" Projecting the economic performance of an adaptation project\\n\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Stakeholder Group:\",\"_key\":\"26407a69638b\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" International Finance Institution\\n\",\"_key\":\"488aa28e18fb\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Impact:\",\"_key\":\"589611c9098e\"},{\"_key\":\"013f45ec3737\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" Unlock finance\\n\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"KPI:\",\"_key\":\"78171a976b72\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" US$ 100 M invested\\n\",\"_key\":\"fff8d6186ad5\"},{\"_key\":\"aa7636c875d5\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Geography:\"},{\"_key\":\"a87145f47204\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" Six primary countries including Ghana, Senegal, Mali, Zambia, Ethiopia, and Kenya\"}],\"_type\":\"block\"},{\"asset\":{\"_ref\":\"image-be046a77a3358ba3784f4d258f6285a768bac54c-1560x1033-jpg\",\"_type\":\"reference\"},\"_type\":\"imageFull\",\"alt\":\"Greenhouse with people inspecting crops\",\"caption\":[{\"_key\":\"3409e6f198f4\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"04256840da6d\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Image credit:\"},{\"text\":\" ©2012CIAT/NeilPalmer\",\"_key\":\"8b4e131b711f\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\"}],\"_key\":\"2565b099353e\"},{\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"c1076280f337\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Useful models\",\"_key\":\"ce71fc60e4510\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"_type\":\"block\"},{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"The World Bank needed to rigorously assess the benefits of a potential new investment to catalyze access and use of new agricultural practices and digital information expansion. However, a lack of comprehensive data or tools across these countries made it difficult to estimate potential impact. To address this, the World Bank collaborated with CGIAR to develop the project’s economic and finance analysis, aiming to provide a detailed analysis of the plausible economic impacts if implemented.\",\"_key\":\"d6d28c9e94050\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"becc9948149f\"},{\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"ed07fd614387\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"10e1a5f5ff760\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"That model, which is the basis of the “Estimating Economic Returns on Adaptation”\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"em\"],\"text\":\" \",\"_key\":\"10e1a5f5ff761\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Spotlight, leverages economic indicators, productivity trends, and project-specific, user-defined inputs offered the World Bank a powerful tool to evaluate the feasibility and potential impact of their investment. With this data-driven evidence, the World Bank was able to advocate effectively for the proposed investments, presenting a compelling case that highlighted the urgent need for action in the face of climate change. The results from the model not only underscored the economic viability of the investment but also its potential to significantly improve agricultural productivity and sustainability in the targeted countries, paving the way for successful funding and implementation of the project.\",\"_key\":\"10e1a5f5ff762\"}]},{\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"6255bfd762c5\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Partners\",\"_key\":\"89f02f6c6fc9\"}]},{\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"c3406ed6c763\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"World Bank, CGIAR Climate Change, Agriculture, and Food Security Program (CCAFS), Alliance of Bioversity-CIAT\",\"_key\":\"9d704e759e580\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"_type\":\"block\"}]},{\"title\":\"Farming systems, economies and livelihood\",\"slug\":\"farming-systems-economies-livelihood\",\"content\":[{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Introduction\",\"_key\":\"c981819de18d\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"cee183135c45\"},{\"children\":[{\"text\":\"About 10% of sub-Saharan Africa’s land area is considered arable. The economic value of agricultural production (i.e., the sum of crop and livestock production values) is unevenly distributed across the continent.\",\"_key\":\"643c3e28c8be0\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"c1f28f319d90\",\"markDefs\":[]},{\"alt\":\"Data Insight, Featured Image: farming systems, economies and livelihood\",\"caption\":[{\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"6bd8be096573\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"text\":\"Image credit:\",\"_key\":\"6b300d96093b0\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"]},{\"_key\":\"6b300d96093b1\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" ©2016 CIAT/NeilPalmer\"}],\"_type\":\"block\"}],\"_key\":\"78c3df0ab947\",\"asset\":{\"_ref\":\"image-0931655d4726520f1ace5b404a100379d4440f72-1560x1041-jpg\",\"_type\":\"reference\"},\"_type\":\"imageFull\"},{\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"5fd32a39a4d1\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"text\":\"High values are concentrated in 2% of the total crop production area\",\"_key\":\"4488a909695c0\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}],\"_type\":\"block\"},{\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"8e2ce624a0da\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"On average, less than half of the arable area generates annual production worth more than USD 500 per hectare. While some areas can produce food crop outputs worth more than USD 5,000 per hectare, such high values are concentrated in 2% of the total crop production area and are likely boosted by access to irrigation and cultivation of high-value crops.\",\"_key\":\"32a445aac8760\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"_type\":\"block\"},{\"_type\":\"imageCaption\",\"alt\":\"Data Insight 2, Map 1: Agricultural value of production, including crop and animals\",\"caption\":[{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"text\":\"Map 1\",\"_key\":\"72c09a0f4e6d0\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"]},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" Agricultural value of production, including crop and animals (international dollar per ha).\",\"_key\":\"c888cb47ba44\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"1bcd2cdf448b\"}],\"_key\":\"97a1ae738bf7\",\"asset\":{\"_ref\":\"image-9e459ae29b818fdc301f127ab2f3395e826566b6-1920x1129-png\",\"_type\":\"reference\"}},{\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"f642806e324f\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"text\":\"Rural poverty and food insecurity are pervasive, especially where non-farm employment options are limited\",\"_key\":\"957dcb4037200\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}]},{\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"97ddd57cedc7\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"With farmers typically cultivating small plots to support their families, rural poverty and food insecurity are pervasive, especially where non-farm employment options are limited. Our analysis of the nationally representative household surveys and agricultural census data from 14 sub-Saharan African countries shows that the majority (83%) of economic value of crop production (i.e., converting the amount of crop produced into money) for cereals, pulses, oil crops, and root crops are generated from farms smaller than five hectares in area.\",\"_key\":\"404199bcf70e0\"}]},{\"_key\":\"4d23a77f62e7\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"303d4452dab20\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Smallholders with less than two hectares generate the economic production values of 48% for cereals\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\"},{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"138d6bac8270\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"In some of the countries, such as Kenya, Malawi, and Rwanda, more than 80% of crop production values come from even smaller fields of less than two hectares. Overall, across 14 countries, these smallholders with less than two hectares generate the economic production values of 48% for cereals, 55% for pulses, 44% for oil crops, and 70% for root crops.\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"b4e2f1fe84e6\"},{\"_type\":\"imageCaption\",\"alt\":\"Data Insight 2, Map 2: climate change impacts on suitability of cereal crops, the density of rural poor, and the value of cereal crop production by smallholders\",\"caption\":[{\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"5ce0b8cdc624\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Map 2\",\"_key\":\"afa5fd0480790\"},{\"text\":\" Three-level (high, medium or low) classification of three variables, including the climate change impacts on the suitability of cereal crops (CC), the density of rural poor (RP), and the value of cereal crop production by smallholders with less than 2 ha farms (VoP). Data in each dimension was normalized as Z-score (low: Z\\u003c-0.67, medium: -0.67\\u003c=Z\\u003c0.67, high: Z\\u003e=0.67).\",\"_key\":\"e20617fe1b75\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}]}],\"_key\":\"35421dfc5d26\",\"asset\":{\"_ref\":\"image-a3dce899199de7a82a46c29add9cd072b7bc82d3-1920x1129-png\",\"_type\":\"reference\"}},{\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"0a9fd348b0f4\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"40806c5b107f0\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Areas should be prioritized for climate change adaptation and their contribution to the country’s economy\"}]},{\"_key\":\"85c26de4adc3\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"We further disaggregated the smallholder-produced crop production values into 10x10 km\",\"_key\":\"0059c209a894\"},{\"_key\":\"b946e1be3a3f\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"super\"],\"text\":\"2\"},{\"text\":\" pixels. This analysis can provide useful insights into the spatial pattern of agricultural production values in each country and, thus, which areas should be prioritized for climate change adaptation and their contribution to the country’s economy. When overlaid with the decreasing suitability of cereal crops projected in 2030 and the prevalence of rural poverty, some hotspot areas were identified across the studied countries. \",\"_key\":\"d5eb5762ce95\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\"},{\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"c0f01f7e8e9a\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Important cereal production in areas of rural poverty coincide disturbingly with negative climate change impacts\",\"_key\":\"288d970067780\"}]},{\"_key\":\"f5450d987a93\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Overall, the analysis shows that the majority (\\u003e80%) of smallholder produce does not face significant climate change impacts by 2030. However, in some countries, important cereal production in areas of rural poverty coincide disturbingly with negative climate change impacts, as seen in Burkina Faso (43% of cereals Value of Production* at risk), Ghana (26%), Niger (21%), Mali (20%) and Nigeria (18%).\",\"_key\":\"e2b2c6185134\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\"}],\"_id\":\"a3bbe45e-7329-42be-833a-255605ad0bf0\",\"_type\":\"insight\"},{\"_id\":\"6aab48e0-35f6-4947-a409-7e82835729c5\",\"_type\":\"insight\",\"title\":\"Pervasive and multiple hazards for agriculture\",\"slug\":\"pervasive-multiple-hazards-for-agriculture\",\"content\":[{\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Introduction\",\"_key\":\"e653aaf9b1ca\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"00324a4d1508\",\"markDefs\":[]},{\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"7c2dc7c60ee4\",\"markDefs\":[{\"_type\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S030691921100114X?via%3Dihub\",\"_key\":\"b949ab91d6d9\"},{\"href\":\"https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/02508060.2018.1516080\",\"_key\":\"ca5a527e5ee9\",\"_type\":\"link\"}],\"children\":[{\"text\":\"In addition to high temperatures, agriculture in sub-Saharan Africa is exposed to a plethora of other hazards. Around 95% of African food production is rainfed (\",\"_key\":\"ab0ae06962da0\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]},{\"text\":\"You et al., 2011\",\"_key\":\"ee50914de26a\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"b949ab91d6d9\"]},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"; \",\"_key\":\"5d26a9d79092\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"ca5a527e5ee9\"],\"text\":\"Xie et al., 2018\",\"_key\":\"0e77cbbe9b2a\"},{\"text\":\"), which means that seasonal excess water and drought play a key role in determining crop productivity.\",\"_key\":\"194692477183\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}],\"_type\":\"block\"},{\"caption\":[{\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"73ef477df934\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Image credit:\",\"_key\":\"f1430e89055c\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" @2011CIAT/NeilPalmer\",\"_key\":\"6b33fd67b7aa\"}]}],\"_key\":\"82409e84118b\",\"asset\":{\"_ref\":\"image-e1fe9bedcc87e2618a92a18c1e31e2544772dd30-1560x1036-jpg\",\"_type\":\"reference\"},\"_type\":\"imageFull\",\"alt\":\"Data Insight, Featured Image: Pervasive and multiple hazards for agriculture\"},{\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"dd5949915924\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"text\":\"Drought can typically affect between 20–30% of agricultural areas in sub-Saharan Africa\",\"_key\":\"7ae5f38b74fe0\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}],\"_type\":\"block\"},{\"_key\":\"d917bda3cd41\",\"markDefs\":[{\"_type\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://journals.ametsoc.org/view/journals/apme/58/6/jamc-d-18-0174.1.xml\",\"_key\":\"cb9da96ef19e\"},{\"_key\":\"f6ebab7a2334\",\"_type\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/09064710701794024\"},{\"_type\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S1470160X15002058?via%3Dihub\",\"_key\":\"bd417f48934e\"},{\"_type\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0034425710002798?via%3Dihub\",\"_key\":\"469a1c026a52\"}],\"children\":[{\"text\":\"Rojas et al. (2011)\",\"_key\":\"8a3f1f4b030c\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"469a1c026a52\"]},{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" estimated that in a given year drought can typically affect between 20–30% of agricultural areas in sub-Saharan Africa, and a single event can reduce production by up to 20% (\",\"_key\":\"9c86ca685f47\",\"_type\":\"span\"},{\"_key\":\"e52140dd1c12\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"cb9da96ef19e\"],\"text\":\"Kim et al., 2019\"},{\"_key\":\"a39053367218\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"). Excess water can also hinder crop productivity through reduced root aeration and increases in root-related diseases (\"},{\"text\":\"Olgun et al., 2008\",\"_key\":\"4dacc01f3bcb\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"f6ebab7a2334\"]},{\"_key\":\"8b0260d1c2c0\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"; \"},{\"_key\":\"a1e887a139c7\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"bd417f48934e\"],\"text\":\"Singh, 2015\"},{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\").\",\"_key\":\"433d21daedf2\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\"},{\"alt\":\"Data Insight 3, Map 1: Total hazard score overlaid with the number of hazards that are considered as being extreme or severe\",\"caption\":[{\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"77189e026711\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Map 1\",\"_key\":\"3d922b51d2460\"},{\"_key\":\"c283a42c067d\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" Total hazard score (total sum of all reclassified hazards) overlaid with the number of hazards that are considered as being extreme or severe. Hazards included are drought, heat and precipitation extremes.\"}],\"_type\":\"block\"}],\"_key\":\"f98b1c2df5e7\",\"asset\":{\"_ref\":\"image-2164a5b824cca7ae706cebb967037d89048f973f-1920x1129-png\",\"_type\":\"reference\"},\"_type\":\"imageCaption\"},{\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"e75c7c7ec433\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Stresses caused by heat, drought and waterlogging are complex\",\"_key\":\"998ecb4bebe60\",\"_type\":\"span\"}]},{\"_key\":\"4c7d65981cc8\",\"markDefs\":[{\"_key\":\"4b9f9a9e6abb\",\"_type\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/17565529.2016.1167659\"}],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Stresses caused by heat, drought and waterlogging are complex because the intensity, timing and duration of these hazards can vary in space and time, sometimes within a relatively small geographic area, \",\"_key\":\"e32070175742\"},{\"marks\":[\"4b9f9a9e6abb\"],\"text\":\"Sonwa et al (2017)\",\"_key\":\"2bde174756c3\",\"_type\":\"span\"},{\"_key\":\"7e8da0eccf78\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" analyze climate risk in nine countries in sub-Saharan Africa and identify a total of 17 specific hazards, all of which cause different types of disruption to agricultural production, including food insecurity and complete abandonment of agricultural activities.\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\"},{\"_key\":\"c4e218ef3894\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"a9c362f2417d\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"The picture is bleak under present-day climate conditions\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\"},{\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"a8f32bde025c\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Map 1 overlays hazard datasets to identify geographies with the incidence of multiple hazards*. The picture is bleak under present-day climate conditions, and climate change is projected to both intensify local hazards and expand the amount of arable land subjected to multiple climate hazards.\",\"_key\":\"c66033f3c339\"}],\"_type\":\"block\"},{\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"a6f848ede41a\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"The co-occurrence of multiple hazards makes these areas increasingly inhospitable\",\"_key\":\"35e3999e6532\"}]},{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"The co-occurrence of multiple hazards makes these areas increasingly inhospitable, and crop production and livestock keeping extremely difficult. As a result, areas have limited human populations and low livestock density, little to no cropland, and livelihoods consist mostly of small-scale subsistence farming.\",\"_key\":\"729f280853fc\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"e06652bcff7a\"},{\"alt\":\"Data Insight 3, Maps 2, 3: Heat stress and drought stress, and Heat stress and climate variability\",\"caption\":[{\"_key\":\"dd29199b0d0d\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Map 2 (left)\",\"_key\":\"fc44d69ed4270\",\"_type\":\"span\"},{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" Heat stress and drought stress, \",\"_key\":\"91c57aa9d52e\",\"_type\":\"span\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Map 3 (right)\",\"_key\":\"28a8c69cc704\"},{\"_key\":\"f4e1d71760b3\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" Heat stress and climate variability\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\"}],\"_key\":\"08090f48359b\",\"asset\":{\"_ref\":\"image-e683f997128bacd034a1dc9b4524f2731628f3dc-1920x618-png\",\"_type\":\"reference\"},\"_type\":\"imageCaption\"},{\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"c2098db3e85a\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Farmers and livestock struggle to cope with hot conditions during the dry months\",\"_key\":\"c7e8e5eabe440\",\"_type\":\"span\"}]},{\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"26c6609a371e\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"In the Sahel, where heat stress is greatest and co-occurs with drought (see Map 2), farmers and livestock struggle to cope with hot conditions during the dry months (especially around April–May). Crops are planted when the rains finally start, and temperatures decrease just enough to bearable levels for farmers to work the land (around late May).\",\"_key\":\"dc37a8d32b9e\"}],\"_type\":\"block\"},{\"_key\":\"97ac8240bd02\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"In many of these areas, livelihoods are on the edge, and migration and conflict are also prevalent\",\"_key\":\"12dca2b58656\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\"},{\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"383c80a2f44c\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"text\":\"However, many dry days at the start of the rainy period can lead to crop failure, leading to food insecurity for those unable to re-plant. During the growing season (June–September), intermittent drought can affect crops, whereas heat stress will typically strike at the end of the season, affecting both crops and farmers as they harvest. In many of these areas, livelihoods are on the edge, and migration and conflict are also prevalent.\",\"_key\":\"20091276d7aa\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}],\"_type\":\"block\"},{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Pasture availability can fluctuate substantially from year to year as a result of drought\",\"_key\":\"37f10c41039d\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"36f5658f7e63\"},{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"A similar picture can be drawn for the Horn of Africa and Southern Africa, where heat stress is less problematic, but drought and climate variability and extremes pose major challenges (see Map 3). In these areas, pastoralism is the main livelihood type either by nomadic herders or partly settled livestock keepers. Pasture availability can fluctuate substantially from year to year as a result of drought.\",\"_key\":\"309d7b8b184e\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"d3d663ad04fa\"},{\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"020ac49e9944\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"In years of extreme drought and low pasture availability, pastoralist groups may experience food insecurity, compete with other nomadic groups and settled farmers for resources and land, or abandon their lands entirely.\",\"_key\":\"8640d7de6488\"}],\"_type\":\"block\"},{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"As climate change intensifies, temperatures increase and rains become less predictable\",\"_key\":\"1f074b9fd1e2\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"66e626ca8768\"},{\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"fa7480ca34c1\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Many other parts of sub-Saharan Africa experience multiple stresses. For example, most of East and Southern Africa, experience moderate levels of heat stress together with severe levels of drought (Map 2). Likewise, many parts of Eastern and Southern Africa experience either mild or severe climate variability and extremes jointly with drought (Map 3).\",\"_key\":\"2a3b4f0c5fab\"}]},{\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"4f92124f016a\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"As climate change intensifies, temperatures increase and rains become less predictable, farmers will require adaptation options and adequate advice and training to be able to move toward a food-secure pathway.\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"b813f4f02db6\",\"markDefs\":[]}]},{\"_type\":\"insight\",\"title\":\"Conflict, rainfall variability and climate security\",\"slug\":\"conflict-rainfall-variability-climate-security\",\"content\":[{\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"98b94c63f56c\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Introduction\",\"_key\":\"e9a1b3dd6d6f0\"}],\"_type\":\"block\"},{\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"It is no coincidence that conflict and instability are a feature of daily life for millions of people subjected to increasingly frequent extreme events. There is a growing body of peer-reviewed literature that has successfully linked at least one climate-related variable (e.g., increased temperatures, changes in rainfall patterns, etc.) with various types of conflict (interpersonal, intergroup, or societal collapse).\",\"_key\":\"2b18fc977528\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"f5a203182bb9\",\"markDefs\":[]},{\"_type\":\"imageFull\",\"alt\":\"Data Insight, Featured Image: Conflict, rainfall variability and climate security\",\"caption\":[{\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"c47c203076a4\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Image credit:\",\"_key\":\"4e77d62e941f\",\"_type\":\"span\"},{\"_key\":\"806d0aae7d9c\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" Patrick Sheperd\"}],\"_type\":\"block\"}],\"_key\":\"edd1f8125839\",\"asset\":{\"_type\":\"reference\",\"_ref\":\"image-0cd10b56133730e35026889d25fea38a3640d519-1560x1169-jpg\"}},{\"_key\":\"a749f34a7ed9\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"b47b6050a9d10\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"While climate change cannot be identified as the only driver, it may increase susceptibility to conflict\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\"},{\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"c00cb19574a1\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Map 1* shows that a total of 47,340 “conflict events” took place across sub-Saharan Africa between 1997–2019, which broadly reflect areas of high precipitation variability. These are primarily located along the Sahel, in North Africa, the Horn of Africa and Southern Africa. While climate change cannot be identified as the only driver, it may increase susceptibility to conflict by amplifying pre-existing inequalities and vulnerabilities. This is underpinned by environmental, economic, social and political influences.\",\"_key\":\"5f074b7984f4\"}],\"_type\":\"block\"},{\"alt\":\"Data Insight 4, Map 1: Coincidence of precipitation variability and fatalities by violence\",\"caption\":[{\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"be4bf030217f\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Map 1 \",\"_key\":\"b1480c7081bb0\"},{\"_key\":\"33393de932c4\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Coincidence of precipitation variability and fatalities by violence.\"}],\"_type\":\"block\"}],\"_key\":\"e7caa14ff6f7\",\"asset\":{\"_type\":\"reference\",\"_ref\":\"image-22cf9a3214175eec5351007c8a59bcfac7679129-1920x1129-png\"},\"_type\":\"imageCaption\"},{\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"17b580cc1ed6\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Rainfall variability and water scarcity are substantial threats\",\"_key\":\"b0a62fdb01b50\"}],\"_type\":\"block\"},{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"From an environmental standpoint, rainfall variability and water scarcity are substantial threats to those whose livelihoods require rainwater for consumption, livestock production and arable agriculture (Salehyan and Hendrix, 2012). This may lead to intercommunal conflict over access to wells and riverbeds (Kahl, 2006), whilst simultaneously forcing pastoralists to sell their livestock and thus become more susceptible to future climate shocks (Theisen, 2017).\",\"_key\":\"5455e404867e\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"1198ddebb899\"},{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Economic shocks in fragile countries can expose young, unemployed people to recruitment by armed groups\",\"_key\":\"3ea6fb862b5c\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"2682624eeac2\"},{\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"414a5fb7498b\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"541278736a85\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Economic growth in poor countries across SSA has been shown to drop by more than 2%, following a 1°C temperature rise. In addition to the indirect impact of reduced harvests on economic activity, this temperature increase may also result in lower labor productivity. In turn, this can lead to rising prices and a heightened risk of violent conflict (Dell et al., 2012). Moreover, economic shocks in fragile countries can expose young, unemployed people to recruitment by armed groups. These may include extremist groups like Al-Shabab in Somalia, which offers cash and other benefits to individuals trapped in poverty and lacking alternative sources of earning a livelihood (Maystadt and Ecker, 2014).\"}],\"_type\":\"block\"},{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Forced sale of livestock due to a climate shock may reduce their mobility, and hence increase their vulnerability\",\"_key\":\"fa51ce08a698\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"505b81d7d00c\"},{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Socially, the mobility changes which climate events demand of pastoralists in particular seem to increase their vulnerability to conflict. Forced sale of livestock due to a climate shock may reduce their mobility, and hence increase their vulnerability to insufficient future rainfall (Maystadt and Ecker, 2014). Alternatively, moving location due to the lack of food, fodder, water and other resources might lead to conflict with settled communities (Theisen, 2012).\",\"_key\":\"d5023e8a3688\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"fc93dd77feb7\"},{\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Preventing pastoralists and semi-pastoralists from being drawn into civil conflict requires carefully targeted programs\",\"_key\":\"8669a12f294b\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"f53e2015846c\",\"markDefs\":[]},{\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"8de62144fa35\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Finally, and unsurprisingly, fragile and unstable political environments make overcoming such difficult situations especially challenging (Theisen, 2017).\",\"_key\":\"6ed68d33ea6f\"}],\"_type\":\"block\"},{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"In spite of these issues, potential solutions exist. As Map 1 shows, the Horn of Africa is stricken by frequent climate hazards (droughts, dry spells and floods), compounded by the fragility of the region’s natural resources. In this region, preventing pastoralists and semi-pastoralists from being drawn into civil conflict requires carefully targeted programs that provide opportunities to participate in credit systems that drive growth in the livestock sector, develop alternative income-earning opportunities, and establish social safety nets.\",\"_key\":\"f82bd355499f\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"2589baa80a3e\"},{\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"64c4a6861b91\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"text\":\"The interactions between climate and the political, social, economic and environmental drivers of conflict are complex\",\"_key\":\"ea3ab6cbe18e\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}],\"_type\":\"block\"},{\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"3eefbe361983\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Furthermore, developing formal insurance mechanisms as well as investments in marketing and infrastructure in the livestock sector can help reduce the pressure to liquidate herds. This can also help prevent the collapse of livestock prices and rapid falls in household incomes that can push people into vulnerable situations, which can then lead to violence.\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"1c3894566cce\",\"markDefs\":[]},{\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"015576cc0707\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"The interactions between climate and the political, social, economic and environmental drivers of conflict are complex and far from fully understood. Continued research and mitigating interventions will be required if further climate-related unrest is to be minimized.\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"cce97009ff7d\",\"markDefs\":[]}],\"_id\":\"32ee6c6b-fe10-4bc4-9eca-d66bb2d40f33\"},{\"content\":[{\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"d71f263f05dd\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Introduction\",\"_key\":\"5caaf56d4e13\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"_type\":\"block\"},{\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"08ea07677933\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Climate change is happening now. The Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change (IPCC) Fifth Assessment Report indicates that global average temperatures have consistently risen in the last 100 years as a result of anthropogenic greenhouse gas emissions.\",\"_key\":\"11c45047cd6c0\"}]},{\"alt\":\"Data Insight, Featured Image: The emergence of a two-degree world\",\"caption\":[{\"children\":[{\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Image credit:\",\"_key\":\"5c5d2fbc6431\",\"_type\":\"span\"},{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" ©2015CIAT/GeorginaSmith\",\"_key\":\"ead7385d6ce6\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"05dffa21d64a\",\"markDefs\":[]}],\"_key\":\"fd88eaa0f842\",\"asset\":{\"_ref\":\"image-17061f22e689d6c2fb5e4ff530f21245b689501f-1560x1036-jpg\",\"_type\":\"reference\"},\"_type\":\"imageFull\"},{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Temperatures and other variables will cross dangerous thresholds\",\"_key\":\"ff46f544d3f60\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"e648a3d6dca6\"},{\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"fe353fe7edeb\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Reported annual global temperature records show that the global average 2017 temperatures are likely between 0.8°C and 1.2°C above pre-industrial levels. The world, therefore, is already on a trajectory of relatively rapid climate change, and temperatures and other variables will cross dangerous thresholds and become harmful for crop and livestock production systems.\",\"_key\":\"d5b5aa8a4e68\"}],\"_type\":\"block\"},{\"_type\":\"imageCaption\",\"alt\":\"Data Insight 5, Map 1: year in which +2oC temperature change is projected to occur during the 21st century\",\"caption\":[{\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"35d1ebdba96f\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"17da6d59b77b0\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Map 1\"},{\"_key\":\"a0259f04870b\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" Year in which +2oC temperature change with respect to pre-industrial levels is projected to occur during the 21st century, for Representative Concentration Pathway (RCP) 8.5.\"}],\"_type\":\"block\"}],\"_key\":\"f9ab91f1984f\",\"asset\":{\"_type\":\"reference\",\"_ref\":\"image-64fc91decba25fcc5dcf71e9312f45d41b06cb54-1920x1129-png\"}},{\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Across sub-Saharan Africa, local +2°C exceedance occurs, at the latest, by 2050\",\"_key\":\"75a16d57ea490\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"2365d53cc68c\",\"markDefs\":[]},{\"markDefs\":[{\"_type\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://www.nature.com/articles/nclimate1261\",\"_key\":\"4fd27fdbe5f5\"}],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Climate projections can be used to determine the times at which local mean temperature exceeds 2°C above pre-industrial levels. Using the Coupled Model Intercomparison Project phase 3 (CMIP3) climate model ensemble, \",\"_key\":\"d771c160e446\",\"_type\":\"span\"},{\"text\":\"Joshi et al. (2011)\",\"_key\":\"8662856b80c1\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"4fd27fdbe5f5\"]},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" suggest that, across sub-Saharan Africa, local +2°C exceedance occurs, at the latest, by 2050. Based on CMIP5 projections focusing on the current emissions trajectory (RCP 8.5) (Map 1)*, the same two-degree target is exceeded across the Sahel before 2030.\",\"_key\":\"17b07a7bba10\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"f29f0f3abf4e\"},{\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Similar exceedance times are projected for most of Southern Africa. Southern West Africa, Central Africa, and East Africa show later projected times of exceedance (up to 2050). The latest exceedance occurs in coastal areas (2050–2060).\",\"_key\":\"e72974b1c94b0\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"9ae3f37fc9c5\",\"markDefs\":[]},{\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"88697b5d94990\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Local temperatures exceed 2°C are expected to lead to drying across most of SSA\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"ebbd3f06a2a1\",\"markDefs\":[]},{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"2ea1811d2770\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"By 2050, virtually all agricultural land and populations in sub-Saharan Africa are projected to experience temperatures that are 2°C warmer than pre-industrial levels. Precipitation changes at the time when local temperatures exceed 2°C are expected to lead to drying across most of SSA, with the exception of East Africa and the central part of the Sahel. Some of these changes are projected to exceed natural variability, thus leading to more severe climates than those experienced by farmers to date (Rojas et al., 2019). \"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"1700cb27682b\"},{\"_type\":\"imageCaption\",\"alt\":\"Data Insight 5, Maps 2, 3: Projections of when maize cropping and bean cropping systems will require transformational change\",\"caption\":[{\"children\":[{\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Map 2 (left)\",\"_key\":\"bb3c90f5ae570\",\"_type\":\"span\"},{\"text\":\" Projections of when maize cropping systems will require transformational change, *Map 3 (right)* Projections of when bean cropping systems will require transformational change.\",\"_key\":\"e169b208d379\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"52dfc20adffe\",\"markDefs\":[]}],\"_key\":\"fe0b5e734738\"},{\"_key\":\"3ac127e54689\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Large commercial and smallholder systems tend to start exceeding the 2°C target earlier than other systems\",\"_key\":\"4b372d9fc8b90\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\"},{\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"f4e74bcf21cf\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Regional variations in the timings of the 2°C exceedance across sub- Saharan Africa will result in variations in such timings between different farming systems. Pastoral, agropastoral (e.g., livestock with millet/sorghum production), irrigated, and large commercial and smallholder systems tend to start exceeding the 2°C target earlier than other systems. Rice-tree crop systems, for example, exceed 2°C later in the century. \"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"cf53a5017e14\",\"markDefs\":[]},{\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"ae1ad31c426d\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"45dc60674da30\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Variations as to when the 2°C limit is crossed for different farming systems, contexts and countries imply different timescales of impact and, therefore, of adaptation actions to be taken.\"}]},{\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"d88c8d0a3a4f\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"cbc208876843\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Investment will be required to create an environment to facilitate adaptation\"}]},{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"text\":\"Maps 2 and 3 show projections of when maize and bean cropping systems become unsuitable and, therefore, require transformational change. For maize, West Africa shows the earliest requirement for transformation, especially toward the Sahel. For beans, substantial areas especially in East and Southern Africa show relatively early (pre-2030) requirements for transformational adaptation. \",\"_key\":\"0b2eb47615ce\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"901d76bd251e\"},{\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"04817ddc69a40\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"In these areas, farmers will experience multiple hazards and, as cropping systems cross dangerous thresholds, they will require support to enable adaptation. In many of these areas, substitution crops are available, and investment will be required to create an environment to facilitate adaptation and take advantage of emerging opportunities.\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"98bcd0f141fa\",\"markDefs\":[]},{\"_key\":\"60f4d96165a1\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"\\n\",\"_key\":\"ce81a9fa80de0\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\"}],\"_id\":\"f3db4c25-bac6-4c08-9a81-543e93b09ec7\",\"_type\":\"insight\",\"title\":\"The emergence of a two-degree world\",\"slug\":\"emergence-of-a-two-degree-world\"},{\"slug\":\"vulnerability-adaptive-capacity-in-climate-change-hotspots\",\"content\":[{\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"64d4d17e2aec\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Introduction\",\"_key\":\"1068f2c9a0ce\"}]},{\"children\":[{\"text\":\"Africa is likely to experience drastic future climate hazards in relation to high temperatures during the growing season, reductions in the length of the growing season, increased climate variability, and greater incidence of floods and droughts.\",\"_key\":\"76747022a7180\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"2893f9452cc4\",\"markDefs\":[]},{\"caption\":[{\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Image credit:\",\"_key\":\"f93c1d6ee4a3\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" ©2012CIAT/NeilPalmer\",\"_key\":\"745e5b055ba8\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"631723c1c3c4\",\"markDefs\":[]}],\"_key\":\"43cebfb2e4e1\",\"asset\":{\"_type\":\"reference\",\"_ref\":\"image-9f0c6d8b9093afa41bdea74169a3b915ef8b9bc9-1560x1033-jpg\"},\"_type\":\"imageFull\",\"alt\":\"Data Insight, Featured Image: Vulnerability and adaptive capacity in climate change hotspots\"},{\"_key\":\"2ee94778a8b3\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"The food sector is highly vulnerable to these climate hazards\",\"_key\":\"2c7055cd47d10\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\"},{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"text\":\"In particular, reductions in the number of reliable crop-growing days per year, and increases in areas in which the average maximum daily temperature moves above 30°C consolidate as critical climate hazards for several major crops in the continent. \",\"_key\":\"60c647880017\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"1b19c0351164\"},{\"_key\":\"2ffb07e88b62\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Given that smallholder farmers practicing rainfed and subsistence agriculture represent a high percentage of the population engaged in farming in Africa, the food sector is highly vulnerable to these climate hazards.\",\"_key\":\"bee989436678\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\"},{\"_type\":\"imageCaption\",\"alt\":\"Data Insight 6, Map 1: Readiness indicator and accessibility to urban markets\",\"caption\":[{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Map 1\",\"_key\":\"5681fe4d03a40\",\"_type\":\"span\"},{\"_key\":\"cb07368cec72\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" “Adaptation domains” defined by the combination of future climate hazards and exposure, mapped for different adaptive capacities*.\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"edcf52178289\"}],\"_key\":\"e7e5334a293e\",\"asset\":{\"_type\":\"reference\",\"_ref\":\"image-314fc91a12ce3c1f9dffb8b5f2837e8703c6f2a7-1920x1129-png\"}},{\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"b984b8e0bf96\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Hazards become particularly dangerous in areas with socio-economic challenges\",\"_key\":\"c5de1497aee1\"}],\"_type\":\"block\"},{\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"4937989b15d5\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"The hazards become particularly dangerous in areas with socio-economic challenges, such as a high prevalence of stunting in children under five years old, and where livelihoods depend on subsistence farming of cereals and roots, including maize-based mixed cropping systems.\",\"_key\":\"ef37da96fdff\"}],\"_type\":\"block\"},{\"_key\":\"26b680bc9c6c\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Properly evaluating, supporting and scaling the most relevant and cost-effective of these options in local contexts remains challenging\",\"_key\":\"af11c17690210\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\"},{\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"c2e36f32837c\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"text\":\"While a variety of adaptation options are available to respond to climate change, properly evaluating, supporting and scaling the most relevant and cost-effective of these options in local contexts remains challenging. In particular, in order to promote innovation for adaptation options, countries will require:\",\"_key\":\"c469a223310c\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}]},{\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"3ebbca1243b9\",\"listItem\":\"number\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"c12d5498f1f0\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"An appropriate business environment that facilitates investment from the private sector;\"}],\"level\":1,\"_type\":\"block\"},{\"listItem\":\"number\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Social stability and institutional arrangements that contribute to reducing investment risks;\\t\",\"_key\":\"930c37f37b61\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"level\":1,\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"943c644608a3\"},{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"f6e32cd7db15\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"High capacity for good governance that reassures investors that invested capital could grow with the help of responsive public services and without significant interruption; \"}],\"level\":1,\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"32577239306d\",\"listItem\":\"number\"},{\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"093eee49c071\",\"listItem\":\"number\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Social conditions that help society make efficient and equitable use of investments, e.g. access to credit and infrastructure for the most vulnerable while ensuring training and information about new adaptation options;\",\"_key\":\"99e05e6e98da\"}],\"level\":1,\"_type\":\"block\"},{\"level\":1,\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"9de50ecff331\",\"listItem\":\"number\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Accessible urban markets, which can unlock the potential for investments and business opportunities, and contribute to more resilient and productive farming systems.\",\"_key\":\"f7996f9631a0\",\"_type\":\"span\"}]},{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"text\":\"Map 1 presents hotspots where this enabling environment is already high and capable of rapidly responding to adaptation options. In these areas, in specific pockets in Southern and humid West Africa, “high readiness” means that the farming population appears well positioned to make effective use of investments for adaptation thanks to a safe and efficient business environment and accessibility to urban markets. These areas constitute fertile ground for investments in adaptation options.\",\"_key\":\"6d66cd65b62e0\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"87524457285f\"},{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"ad47a44910520\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Many adaptation options are suitable in the areas shown in Map 1. These range from the adoption of crop varieties that can tolerate stresses, such as water submergence, drought, high temperature, and pests and diseases to fundamentally changing farming systems, such as shifting from crops to livestock, shifting to different livestock types, or shifting to different crops. But for adaptation to be effectively implemented, “high readiness” (red, dark blue areas) would be fundamental to ensuring that small-scale farmers rapidly adopt new technologies and practices. Where readiness is low (light orange and light blue areas), major investments are required to raise farmers’ adaptive capacity. In areas of high accessibility to urban markets, adaptation can quickly trigger positive shifts in farming systems as local economies can be highly responsive to consumer demand.\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"652b95b24526\"}],\"_id\":\"a759a957-34a4-4637-9453-ba012f7b78ba\",\"_type\":\"insight\",\"title\":\"Vulnerability and adaptive capacity in climate change hotspots\"},{\"title\":\"Emerging opportunities for farmers – and research\",\"slug\":\"emerging-opportunities-for-farmers-and-research\",\"content\":[{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Introduction \",\"_key\":\"fabb2c8a90dd\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"3b888c1efb4c\"},{\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Projections indicate that, without adaptation, African agricultural productivity will likely decrease during the 21st century as a result of climate impacts, increasing the risk of food and nutritional insecurity throughout the continent (\",\"_key\":\"da7ad95adae40\",\"_type\":\"span\"},{\"text\":\"Challinor et al., 2014\",\"_key\":\"5dc519023391\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"285bcae9443f\"]},{\"text\":\"; \",\"_key\":\"ae10f866a2c0\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]},{\"_key\":\"532053c8a6a1\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"8472ab83d4a0\"],\"text\":\"Müller et al., 2011\"},{\"text\":\"; \",\"_key\":\"71d0c4a45d3f\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]},{\"marks\":[\"2ae230437885\"],\"text\":\"van Ittersum et al., 2016\",\"_key\":\"394bc9f0ff7c\",\"_type\":\"span\"},{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\").\",\"_key\":\"5e5d54afabb0\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"bc458ddf2ec6\",\"markDefs\":[{\"href\":\"https://www.nature.com/articles/nclimate2153\",\"_key\":\"285bcae9443f\",\"_type\":\"link\"},{\"_type\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://www.pnas.org/doi/full/10.1073/pnas.1015078108\",\"_key\":\"8472ab83d4a0\"},{\"_type\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://www.pnas.org/doi/full/10.1073/pnas.1610359113\",\"_key\":\"2ae230437885\"}]},{\"asset\":{\"_type\":\"reference\",\"_ref\":\"image-4362005292dadb19ec373ecf3447f6854a4b9420-1560x1036-jpg\"},\"_type\":\"imageFull\",\"alt\":\"Data Insight, Featured Image: Emerging opportunities for farmers and research\",\"_key\":\"92307c854b61\"},{\"_key\":\"d5cc5d225b7f\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"An opportunity for new livelihood strategies, and market growth\",\"_key\":\"c72a6e994bc30\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\"},{\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"24ecbb5d058e\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"But while changes in climate can have negative impacts on the suitability of certain crops in some areas, the opposite may be true for other crops in other areas. This presents an opportunity for new livelihood strategies, and market growth. Making the most of these opportunities is just as important as adapting to the negative impacts of climate change. \"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"298d877db346\",\"markDefs\":[]},{\"_key\":\"1e65284ba4c1\",\"asset\":{\"_ref\":\"image-82e72946fd5121b9257d622841e7458924f927b5-1920x1129-png\",\"_type\":\"reference\"},\"_type\":\"imageCaption\",\"alt\":\"Data Insight 7, Map 1: Suitability and market access of all crops\",\"caption\":[{\"_key\":\"977a9e55895d\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Map 1\",\"_key\":\"0707148434d00\",\"_type\":\"span\"},{\"text\":\" Where suitability for crop cultivation is projected to increase, there may be emerging opportunities for smallholder farmers. Shown are different levels of opportunities layered with accessibility to markets. Blue indicates where market accessibility is high (less than six hours of travel time), while orange-red indicates limited accessibility to markets (more than 6 hours of travel time). Emerging opportunities are categorized from 1 (highest risk) to 5 (lowest risk), based on their projected suitability under climate change in the 2030s. Light gray areas indicate areas in which crops are suitable in the baseline and either remain suitable or decrease suitability by 2030. Gray-striped polygons highlight protected areas. Dark gray areas are those in which no rainfed cropping is possible.\",\"_key\":\"124ba283c396\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\"}]},{\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"d934db8295e0\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"The vast majority of these opportunities are in areas considered to have relatively high market access\",\"_key\":\"8e6e1f6fe2860\"}]},{\"_key\":\"018544d22b04\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Map 1 shows potential opportunities that emerge from increases in crop suitability*. A number of areas emerge across sub-Saharan Africa. Notably, the increased rainfall of the eastern Sahel and East Africa increases the suitability of some (but not all) of the crops, which move mostly from being unsuitable to marginally suitable, or from marginally to moderately suitable.\",\"_key\":\"2bab29a3e8b8\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\"},{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"87e0cdc153540\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"The vast majority of these opportunities are in areas considered to have relatively high market access and where there are no major land-use restrictions, such as high forest cover or protected areas. Highland areas in Kenya and Ethiopia, however, see increases in average crop suitability in many areas that are either protected or have high forest cover.\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"a86637425b80\"},{\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"32b980977acf\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Analysis of individual crops reveals what the opportunities are. Map 2 shows hotspots where farmers could benefit from expanding cultivation of cassava.\",\"_key\":\"68e4b2c0f1fe0\",\"_type\":\"span\"}]},{\"_key\":\"e5a86da794e0\",\"asset\":{\"_type\":\"reference\",\"_ref\":\"image-3b5de7a8729f20e67d422fd8e037fd86d9d8ea2e-1920x618-png\"},\"_type\":\"imageCaption\",\"alt\":\"Data Insight 7, Maps 2, 3: Suitability and market access of cassava, wheat\",\"caption\":[{\"_key\":\"d3ae842d42b7\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"b9310f7591fa0\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Map 2 (left)\"},{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" Suitability and market access of cassava, \",\"_key\":\"11ba09dc11b1\",\"_type\":\"span\"},{\"_key\":\"3a30618ada02\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Map 3 (right)\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" Suitability and market access of wheat\",\"_key\":\"c1ce14a321ff\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\"}]},{\"_key\":\"91bf9898e02d\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Cassava production might be an excellent opportunity for improving rural livelihoods\",\"_key\":\"64adf6b04ab40\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\"},{\"_key\":\"94433e1b0ed4\",\"markDefs\":[{\"_type\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1002/jsfa.8287\",\"_key\":\"20023b3449a9\"},{\"_type\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0959652618322790?via%3Dihub\",\"_key\":\"f9fbbd712627\"},{\"_type\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s12042-012-9096-7\",\"_key\":\"a0c235b29d38\"},{\"_key\":\"0707239661ac\",\"_type\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://doi.org/10.3354/cr0006153\"}],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"In sub-Saharan Africa, cassava is primarily a food crop, although it has substantial untapped potential for starch production for industrial use (\",\"_key\":\"319c15b5055c\",\"_type\":\"span\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"20023b3449a9\"],\"text\":\"Li et al. 2017\",\"_key\":\"b325151625b2\"},{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"; \",\"_key\":\"ad6976db0d17\",\"_type\":\"span\"},{\"_key\":\"b9bd1d0da091\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"f9fbbd712627\"],\"text\":\"Poku et al., 2018\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"). In Zimbabwe, where we identify significant opportunities emerging for cassava, Kleih (1995) estimated starch demand to be in the region of 7,700 tonnes of chips, and demand for ethanol equivalent to 240,000 tonnes of fresh roots. Cassava has also been identified as a source of calories for subsistence farmers in marginal areas where most other crops fail (\",\"_key\":\"696315d10d59\"},{\"_key\":\"fc44604f61e4\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"a0c235b29d38\"],\"text\":\"Jarvis et al., 2012\"},{\"_key\":\"20d3f203a2d4\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"; \"},{\"marks\":[\"0707239661ac\"],\"text\":\"Kamukondiwa, 1996\",\"_key\":\"eb454d09f701\",\"_type\":\"span\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\").\",\"_key\":\"15136aa30e6b\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\"},{\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"If these areas do not disturb strategic ecosystems suited for conservation and forestry, then cassava production might be an excellent opportunity for improving rural livelihoods. Furthermore, existing or new cassava farmers will need relatively easy access to inputs, seeds, and financing in order to foster enterprise. Perhaps most importantly, they will need access to markets with sufficient demand to make the business opportunity attractive. Any such areas with low travel time to major cities would likely be hotspots for such investments.\",\"_key\":\"3d301c1325df0\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"cdf2f7e4a7d5\",\"markDefs\":[]},{\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"4ab0b2e5a334\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"It would be crucial to understand and map out the existence of the necessary conditions for expanding production of these crops\",\"_key\":\"2852e38ab0340\"}],\"_type\":\"block\"},{\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Strategic hotspots for the development of new value chains and the growth of agricultural markets are similar for cassava, chickpea, beans, pigeon pea, soybean and sesame seed that are mostly located in South Africa, Botswana and Zimbabwe. For crops such as rainfed wheat, on the other hand, which primarily experience reductions in crop suitability, our model-based estimates indicate that there would be few opportunities for expanding cultivation. \",\"_key\":\"935104c52a83\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"ef260d2bc6ef\",\"markDefs\":[]},{\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"1a5a79ff1ad7\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Further research would be needed to better understand the implications of the opportunities for improving rural livelihoods in these specific zones. In particular, it would be crucial to understand and map out the existence of the necessary conditions for expanding production of these crops. Such conditions would include access to credit and appropriate infrastructure, and availability of seed, other inputs, training and effective extension systems.\",\"_key\":\"a7b4690783e20\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"_type\":\"block\"}],\"_id\":\"3db182c9-2257-4979-b1a5-b50e70dee6a3\",\"_type\":\"insight\"},{\"slug\":\"options-for-adaptation\",\"content\":[{\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Introduction\",\"_key\":\"31b218b21f95\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"7310b96c6ddf\",\"markDefs\":[]},{\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"da0b36783657\",\"markDefs\":[{\"_type\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://www.mdpi.com/2071-1050/11/5/1372\",\"_key\":\"adc74de53006\"}],\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"82b7241beaae0\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Despite the unprecedented challenges smallholder farmers in Africa are facing due to climate change, there are many options available to help them adapt (\"},{\"marks\":[\"adc74de53006\"],\"text\":\"Loboguerrero et al., 2019\",\"_key\":\"8f54deea1b0d\",\"_type\":\"span\"},{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\").\",\"_key\":\"d00606ad04c9\",\"_type\":\"span\"}]},{\"_type\":\"imageFull\",\"alt\":\"Data Insight, Featured Image: Options for adaptation\",\"caption\":[{\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"8b160f5957cc\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Image credit:\",\"_key\":\"5b671cab47f2\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" ©2012CIAT/NeilPalmer\",\"_key\":\"bf786fe1f6db\"}],\"_type\":\"block\"}],\"_key\":\"4d86d86aa296\",\"asset\":{\"_type\":\"reference\",\"_ref\":\"image-a15843b18e45fcb23f3be1f676ed62b437d4d74f-1560x1033-jpg\"}},{\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Suitability of each adaptation option will depend on the farming system, climate, soils and social context\",\"_key\":\"11bfc09c054c0\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"62bbc9df7f84\",\"markDefs\":[]},{\"markDefs\":[{\"_type\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0959378009000156?via%3Dihub\",\"_key\":\"61749c29b7b8\"}],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Adaptation options run the gamut from farm management practices (e.g., which crops and varieties to plant, which inputs to use, how to prepare the land, or even how the harvest is stored) to services that farmers can access (e.g., climate information, extension, insurance, credit and loans). However, the suitability of each adaptation option will depend on the farming system, climate, soils and social context (\",\"_key\":\"c5d20646f9d0\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"61749c29b7b8\"],\"text\":\"Deressa et al., 2009\",\"_key\":\"659f9a699a5e\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\").\",\"_key\":\"45bdc115a307\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"872bf1801a8c\"},{\"caption\":[{\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"beee294524730\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Map 1\"},{\"_key\":\"9736e5a64b3d\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" Number of adaptation options (out of the 28 modeled) that will be suitable in 2030 under RCP 8.5.\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"322ba3768cea\",\"markDefs\":[]}],\"_key\":\"42983cb0e30f\",\"asset\":{\"_type\":\"reference\",\"_ref\":\"image-ddd0f9830a3172f700500604bb324a75eab42ef1-1920x1129-png\"},\"_type\":\"imageCaption\",\"alt\":\"Data Insight 8, Map 1: Adaptation options that will be suitable in 2030 under RCP 8.5.\"},{\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"ec78826f64e1\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Across arable parts of Africa, all places had 8 or more options projected to be suitable in the future\",\"_key\":\"600a8d46fda10\"}],\"_type\":\"block\"},{\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"67efc96110da\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"text\":\"Map 1 shows the number of adaptation options (out of the 28 modeled) that will be suitable in 2030 under a high-emissions climate change scenario*. Across arable parts of Africa, all places had 8 or more options projected to be suitable in the future, while others had more than 20. Some options were found to be broadly suitable across many different farming contexts.\",\"_key\":\"2070185f6a7e\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}],\"_type\":\"block\"},{\"alt\":\"Data Insight 8, Adaptation Options 1, 2: Zia pits in Niger, Conservation Agriculture in Malawi\",\"caption\":[{\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"977c1dd2f58c0\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Image credits:\"},{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" M. Tall/CCAFS (left), T. Samson/CIMMYT (right)\",\"_key\":\"c5b368f3a1ec\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"0fae84b9c834\",\"markDefs\":[]}],\"_key\":\"b493c4e394e3\",\"asset\":{\"_ref\":\"image-4722b36ece813a10d5e818710961e6e2e216340e-2000x872-png\",\"_type\":\"reference\"},\"_type\":\"imageCaption\"},{\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"c7b7e65331cf\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Many of these options are practices that improve soil health\",\"_key\":\"c5b26cdea8510\",\"_type\":\"span\"}]},{\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"6d4095697703\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Many of these options are practices that improve soil health, including the addition of soil nutrients from organic and inorganic sources, crop rotation and fallowing, which have been identified as a key component to achieving food security in Africa (Sánchez, 2010). \",\"_key\":\"978279d31975\"}],\"_type\":\"block\"},{\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"20fbddf484ad\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"For example, the addition of organic and inorganic inputs was projected to increase crop yields and improve soil conditions in 91% and 88% of arable land respectively, across all farming systems. Rotating maize with other crops such as legumes was also broadly suitable for increasing maize yields in 2030 and was found to be suitable in 98% of arable areas in sub-Saharan Africa.\",\"_key\":\"6bd670e258a60\"}]},{\"alt\":\"Data Insight 8, Adaptation Options 3: Drought-tolerant maize varieties in Nigeria\",\"caption\":[{\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"920faa7355b4\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Image credit:\",\"_key\":\"156813710a520\",\"_type\":\"span\"},{\"text\":\" A. Wangalachi/CIMMYT\",\"_key\":\"7a1f702ba2fe\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}]}],\"_key\":\"b6c570b1ef1e\",\"asset\":{\"_ref\":\"image-27968be54d1d39061acbd0776cdad284f37a4b8b-2000x872-png\",\"_type\":\"reference\"},\"_type\":\"imageCaption\"},{\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Although some practices may show low suitability because they do not generally increase crop yields by at least 15%, they may have other benefits\",\"_key\":\"c3df9774a5210\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"e989e630324e\",\"markDefs\":[]},{\"_key\":\"56d5d6783f0b\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Other adaptation options have narrower niches, or agroecological conditions where they are suitable. For example, reducing soil tillage by using direct seeding methods and other techniques, when practiced alone, generally does not significantly increase maize yields and may even reduce them, particularly in humid areas (Pittelkow et al., 2015). \",\"_key\":\"d007d71277d9\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\"},{\"_key\":\"7b75b2cf91cd\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"text\":\"In our analysis, we found reduced tillage alone to be broadly unsuitable for increasing maize yields in 2030. Similarly, the agroforestry practice of alley cropping, where maize or other crops are planted between rows (or alleys) of trees, was found to be suitable on less than 10% of arable land in sub-Saharan Africa. Although some practices may show low suitability because they do not generally increase crop yields by at least 15%, they may have other benefits such as improving soil health, enabling farmers to diversify their income streams, or capturing carbon. These can reduce their vulnerability or exposure to climate change hazards.\",\"_key\":\"d24f64ed3f660\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\"},{\"_type\":\"imageCaption\",\"alt\":\"Data Insight 8, Adaptation Options 4, 5: Agroforestry in Kenya, Intercropping in Cameroon\",\"caption\":[{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"b19bfc3014bb\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Image credits:\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" Neil Palmer/CIAT(left) IITA (right)\",\"_key\":\"31b3ac9ce2db\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"39fd74998f9f\"}],\"_key\":\"09c02be0b528\",\"asset\":{\"_ref\":\"image-5a056f35929e34327907fcbf6e853e4c3312cd75-2000x920-png\",\"_type\":\"reference\"}},{\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"250cbec7db6e\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"text\":\"Agroecological suitability should be combined with adaptive capacity analysis \",\"_key\":\"16f353d5a67d0\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}]},{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"text\":\"The agroecological suitability of a technology is only the first step in adapting food systems to climate change. The adoption of these technologies by smallholder farmers depends on a diverse array of social factors. Access to information, availability of resources such as wealth or credit, and security of land tenure may be key enabling factors in Africa (Arslan et al., 2020). Thus, agroecological suitability should be combined with adaptive capacity analysis to determine the best-bet adaptation options for a given context. \",\"_key\":\"e73d964cfd31\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"0f6930d5151d\"},{\"_key\":\"6554483bfc08\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Evidence shows that all farming systems in sub-Saharan Africa are likely to have many suitable adaptation options now and under future climate change scenarios. While the adaptation options modeled are based on studies of many locations across a range of contexts in Africa, there may be many more that are suitable for which we do not currently have data.\",\"_key\":\"b0d057aa23fe0\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\"}],\"_id\":\"87b34ef8-8ff5-4291-8681-77caf81bf15b\",\"_type\":\"insight\",\"title\":\"Options for adaptation\"},{\"_type\":\"insight\",\"title\":\"A last resort: switching to alternative crops\",\"slug\":\"a-last-resort-switching-to-alternative-crops\",\"content\":[{\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"a4540ac085a2\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"text\":\"Introduction\",\"_key\":\"f7745be2b3010\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}]},{\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"If farmers’ first lines of defense against climate hazards are insufficient or not accessible, then a “last resort” for adaptation could be to switch to an alternative crop. This represents a move from additive or synergistic incremental changes to more transformational change.\",\"_key\":\"02c964ae7417\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"2f6265d228db\",\"markDefs\":[]},{\"_type\":\"imageFull\",\"alt\":\"Data Insight, Featured Image: A last resort: switching to alternative crops\",\"caption\":[{\"_key\":\"bde4008cb34b\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Image credit:\",\"_key\":\"3729feff5396\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" ©2016CIAT/GeorginaSmith\",\"_key\":\"415945cd7db3\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\"}],\"_key\":\"497c8990c11a\",\"asset\":{\"_ref\":\"image-9973e6c28f6e25b6eaf1046e759f6d2e07c60ca3-1560x1040-jpg\",\"_type\":\"reference\"}},{\"_key\":\"8df11893ad1f\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Asking a farmer to change crops, is likely to be more difficult to implement than incremental change\",\"_key\":\"8b1f54332ca50\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\"},{\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"7256f5f5dd98\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"text\":\"We deliberately use the phrase “last resort” because transformational change, such as asking a farmer to change crops, is likely to be more difficult to implement than incremental change. Switching to a new crop brings risk and demands increased knowledge compared to working with familiar crops. The resistance to adoption of new crops is, therefore, likely to be higher than changing the way existing crops are grown. New crops may also require supply chains and markets to be developed if that commodity is not already grown in an area. \",\"_key\":\"5e52f36fc58d\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}],\"_type\":\"block\"},{\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"a171d9c5c996\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Nevertheless, common bean is a valuable and nutritionally important crop that is highly sensitive to climate change. Unless drastic measures are taken to reduce greenhouse gas emissions, there may be areas where the crop becomes unviable despite our best adaptation efforts.\",\"_key\":\"7836a57a9dec0\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"_type\":\"block\"},{\"_key\":\"cbb1574694de\",\"asset\":{\"_ref\":\"image-7e496f1ad47386c19e32b1f80b5b8ff66cbdef61-1920x1129-png\",\"_type\":\"reference\"},\"_type\":\"imageCaption\",\"alt\":\"Data Insight 9, Map 1: Number of alternative legumes\",\"caption\":[{\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"168d35326198\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"259f1d9b05a50\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Map 1\"},{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" Number of alternative legumes\",\"_key\":\"c04aa9de3d95\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"_type\":\"block\"}]},{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"There are alternatives, although the number of suitable species varies\",\"_key\":\"116b64a294830\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"d1877b6d99c0\"},{\"_key\":\"c00e79a386c7\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"text\":\"The most severe declines in total bean suitability area are seen in Uganda (27.3%), Zimbabwe (26.4%), Tanzania (20.1%) and the Democratic Republic of Congo (DRC) (15.7%). Fortunately, of the seven other legumes modeled, there are alternatives, although the number of suitable species varies. Uganda and DRC typically have six or seven alternatives to choose from, but southwest Zimbabwe and South Africa only have two or three.*\",\"_key\":\"7342a1af1283\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\"},{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Legumes with higher heat tolerance and lower rainfall needs, such as pigeonpea and cowpea, appear to be almost universal substitutes in the zone of common bean decline, whereas soybean and groundnut appear to be the least suitable alternatives. We can zoom into nations and smaller areas to see which legumes work in specific contexts. In South Africa, only cowpea, lentil and pigeonpea are viable alternatives whilst, in Uganda, these species are joined by chickpea, broad bean, groundnut and soybean.\",\"_key\":\"a40d0a8eecd80\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"1dc4eb9fde5b\"},{\"_key\":\"4028b0b0a84f\",\"asset\":{\"_type\":\"reference\",\"_ref\":\"image-fc76f20f18c87ee7d8917dafd07c63fb3ee3d14e-1920x1129-png\"},\"_type\":\"imageCaption\",\"alt\":\"Data Insight 9, Map 2: Predicted decline in common bean suitability\",\"caption\":[{\"_key\":\"9dfab1215ecd\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Map 2\",\"_key\":\"34de17a4d9df0\"},{\"_key\":\"57496a97a76a\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" Predicted decline in common bean suitability\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\"}]},{\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"0dd522080553\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"There are many factors other than climate that need to be considered when evaluating the suitability of alternative crops\",\"_key\":\"6a06212aa2d90\"}],\"_type\":\"block\"},{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"text\":\"Where farming system transformation is needed, there are many factors other than climate that need to be considered when evaluating the suitability of alternative crops. Commercial farmers will evaluate a crop based on its profitability (e.g., yield, market price, access and volatility), practicality (e.g., access to competitive varieties and compatibility with farm infrastructure) and reliability (vulnerability of the crop to pests, diseases and climate hazards). For smallholder farmers, nutritional and cultural factors will also be important considerations, especially if the focal crop is a significant part of their household diet. If an alternative crop yields fewer calories and/or macronutrients per unit area, does not taste as good or requires more effort to prepare or process, then its value as a substitute crop will diminish.\",\"_key\":\"fed04fb52bb6\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"978a6b1df6d9\"}],\"_id\":\"e6c402bc-2128-45a8-ab0c-c7259278072e\"},{\"content\":[{\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"750b0b98262a\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Introduction\",\"_key\":\"152bc341b0ae\"}]},{\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"e7d84872e1aa\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"text\":\"Since the 1970s, thousands of agricultural trials and research studies have been conducted in Africa, testing the ways in which changes in farm management practices lead to changes in yields, farmers’ incomes or soil health. This research forms the basis of our knowledge of the adaptation options that will work in different locations, both now and under different climate change scenarios (Rosenstock et al., 2016). However, the research is not evenly distributed across the continent. When we map where those studies have been undertaken, we can see areas in which it is densely clustered (“data jungles”) and large areas where there has been virtually no research (“data deserts”).\",\"_key\":\"c647bfbd0b090\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}]},{\"_type\":\"imageFull\",\"alt\":\"Data Insight, Featured Image: Data deserts and data jungles\",\"_key\":\"adc8bf914158\",\"asset\":{\"_type\":\"reference\",\"_ref\":\"image-0d3006b74c73b80d823d611aea40dea02f0af6ad-1560x929-jpg\"}},{\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"8839be39b50c\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"3c1f1b4c24f30\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"About 25% of the agricultural research in Africa has been undertaken in the maize-mixed farming system\"}],\"_type\":\"block\"},{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"0fa64dd0dd8d\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"DATA JUNGLES\\n\"},{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Several countries are rich in research data, including Nigeria, Ethiopia, Kenya, Malawi and Zimbabwe, reflecting the history of agricultural research on the continent (Roseboom and Flaherty, 2016). About 25% of the agricultural research in Africa has been undertaken in the maize-mixed farming system, semi-arid systems where maize is the staple crop, but where other crops and livestock are also produced. \",\"_key\":\"3c1f1b4c24f31\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"c0a89f8f0d3d\"},{\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"48f4668c82760\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"This wealth of knowledge is also reflected in the proportion of data on maize, which accounts for 45.6% of the available agricultural research data across the continent. We also have a good deal of knowledge about agropastoral systems, which tend to be found in semi-arid areas.\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"134abf91d6c8\",\"markDefs\":[]},{\"asset\":{\"_ref\":\"image-be64d8de3c289faa89d0e11210032305565f9da3-1920x1129-png\",\"_type\":\"reference\"},\"_type\":\"imageCaption\",\"alt\":\"Data Insight 10, Map 1: Data deserts and data jungles\",\"caption\":[{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Map 1\",\"_key\":\"90cfde5c9a730\"},{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" Data deserts and data jungles\",\"_key\":\"4b6609cd3fdf\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"1a2830e6b859\"}],\"_key\":\"423d70e3c1ff\"},{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"af09b456f67d0\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Around three-quarters of the available data contains information on nutrient management practices \"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"e277ddaa0409\"},{\"_key\":\"b443399fe218\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"d92ce2adab73\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Another well-studied agroecological zone in Africa is the highland perennial system, characterized by diverse crops such as banana, coffee, tea, and dairy production. This system supports the highest rural population density of any farming system in Africa and more than 15% of the available research has been done in this system.*\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\"},{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"e466fcd003ec0\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"We know a lot about some adaptation options and agricultural practices. Around three-quarters of the available data contains information on nutrient management practices, particularly the use of inputs such as inorganic and organic fertilizers. Often, these practices are undertaken in combination with other technologies. Practices that focus on improving soil health, such as mulching, reduced tillage, or intercropping also make up a large portion of our knowledge base, at 46% of available data.\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"c90701d929a3\"},{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"70f96f2a21110\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Agricultural research has focused on cereal crops, neglecting others that are critical for smallholder nutrition and food security\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"c9f785c744a7\"},{\"_key\":\"cde08af79156\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"text\":\"DATA DESERTS\\n\",\"_key\":\"d40c92a89c9f\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"]},{\"_key\":\"70f96f2a21111\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Despite the wealth of agricultural data available in some parts of Africa, there are still large gaps, particularly for some farming systems. While a large proportion of Africa’s population lives in humid coastal and lowland areas, farming systems in these areas represent just 13.5% of the available data. \"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\"},{\"_key\":\"49741b831f90\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Key staple crops in these systems are also under-represented, with cassava accounting for 3% of the data and bananas less than 0.1%. Much of the agricultural research has focused on cereal crops, neglecting others that are critical for smallholder nutrition and food security. Vegetables comprise only 2% of the available data, with the majority of that data focused on marketable vegetables such as tomato and onions. Indigenous vegetables or other horticultural crops with high nutritional value and that women farmers generally have more involvement with (World Bank/FAO/ IFAD, 2009) are virtually absent from the research.\",\"_key\":\"8c8f99dcc31b0\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\"},{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Livestock accounted for less than 3% of the available data\",\"_key\":\"fd123461df600\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"4bb564bfdadc\"},{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Livestock is another critical component of many smallholder agriculture systems, providing a key source of nutrition, income, and labor saving for households. Livestock systems are also threatened by climate change (Thornton et al., 2009). Despite their importance in smallholder agriculture, livestock accounted for less than 3% of the available data, with cattle and goat production comprising half of that information and milk and eggs about a quarter each.\",\"_key\":\"7da223bf806f\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"2d3d08d6f6f0\"},{\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Data is largely concentrated in a few key commodities, such as maize, and in semi-arid systems\",\"_key\":\"845eae030d200\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"ca0b75be39f7\",\"markDefs\":[]},{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"text\":\"TARGETING KNOWLEDGE GAPS\\n\",\"_key\":\"3e2dedbf94b2\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"]},{\"_key\":\"845eae030d201\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"There is a wealth of data available on the performance of many practices and technologies for improving agricultural productivity and adapting to climate change in Africa. However, that data is largely concentrated in a few key commodities, such as maize, and in semi-arid systems. Millions of smallholder farmers are located in “data deserts” where there is little information available on the key crops and the key environmental challenges they face. \"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"0ebe267c5d8f\"},{\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"3044de8089c9\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Future research should target these knowledge gaps and focus on under-studied farming systems, nutritionally critical crops and livestock, as well as crops more often thought of as “women’s crops.”\",\"_key\":\"fda5870bed620\"}],\"_type\":\"block\"}],\"_id\":\"9f1ec45a-1d26-41a2-ab28-1ad3a7505efe\",\"_type\":\"insight\",\"title\":\"Data deserts and data jungles\",\"slug\":\"data-deserts-and-data-jungles\"},{\"title\":\"Climate Payouts to Smallholders\",\"prototype\":true,\"slug\":\"climatePayouts\",\"content\":[{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"8e37e4e0e0de\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"This tool analyzes how climate-driven extreme weather, particularly droughts and floods, affects farms and farmer livelihoods across Africa, with a focus on identifying where, how many, and which types of farms are most likely to experience losses now and in the future. Using farm size distributions, historical data, and climate model ensembles (CMIP6) under different emissions scenarios, it estimates the probability of loss and lost revenue by farm size and region, projects changes in the number of farms to 2050, and quantifies how many farms may require financial support following extreme events. The tool is designed to support policy and program planning by providing evidence on the scale and distribution of agricultural loss and damage, highlighting the particular vulnerability of smallholders, and informing the design of farmer assistance, insurance, adaptation, and risk-reduction strategies under climate change.\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"4a6d55daaa6f\"}],\"featuredTags\":[{\"name\":\"Hazards\",\"slug\":{\"current\":\"hazards\",\"_type\":\"slug\"},\"_id\":\"d4f0b388-28d1-4707-86cb-3c89d9903357\"},{\"_id\":\"ff9a72cf-1da2-4c34-aa0b-5585547602d9\",\"name\":\"Projections\",\"slug\":{\"_type\":\"slug\",\"current\":\"projections-fr\"}}],\"_id\":\"7e3324ed-f74f-4019-aeb1-b267b0da95c5\",\"_type\":\"spotlight\"},{\"slug\":\"aaa-csaips\",\"content\":[{\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"769c8a4c0684\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Synopsis\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"4e6d15ad5011\",\"markDefs\":[]},{\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"f3b5e1599515\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Data underlying the Atlas helped stakeholders understand upcoming hazards, agricultural exposure, and the economics of response options in four African countries, outlining adaptation rationale and responses.\",\"_key\":\"29fc27d7aba40\",\"_type\":\"span\"}]},{\"children\":[{\"text\":\"Use Case:\",\"_key\":\"edd5e8ef8f07\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"]},{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" Linking climate risks to responses to inform effective and efficient programming\\n\",\"_key\":\"8689078c419c\",\"_type\":\"span\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Stakeholder Group:\",\"_key\":\"37fb35a04c29\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" Government, International Finance Institution, NGO\\n\",\"_key\":\"c47348eaf136\"},{\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Impact:\",\"_key\":\"61ede886ee4f\",\"_type\":\"span\"},{\"_key\":\"38f6bf93849b\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" Shape plans\\n\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"KPI:\",\"_key\":\"ff2498ed434b\"},{\"text\":\" 4 plans influenced\\n\",\"_key\":\"c38a32862a1f\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Geography:\",\"_key\":\"105a69b9aae5\"},{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" Ghana, Burkina Faso, Mali, Côte d’Ivoire\",\"_key\":\"875d36de2642\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"85e0d0db787a\",\"markDefs\":[]},{\"_type\":\"imageFull\",\"alt\":\"Farmland hills in Uganda\",\"caption\":[{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"7987dc7d228b\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Image credit:\"},{\"text\":\" ©2009CIAT/NeilPalmer\",\"_key\":\"9c203205b2f8\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"126d6e6ae634\"}],\"_key\":\"e5e2830754ea\",\"asset\":{\"_ref\":\"image-ec4170fc1028901d6328599249b2b9b2d9de059c-1560x1036-jpg\",\"_type\":\"reference\"}},{\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"663c3bd5aa01\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Connecting risks to economically-viable responses\",\"_key\":\"421d998b7d4b0\"}]},{\"markDefs\":[{\"_key\":\"d7f9dd0811e6\",\"_type\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://www.worldbank.org/en/topic/agriculture/publication/climate-smart-agriculture-investment-plans-bringing-climate-smart-agriculture-to-life\"}],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"At CoP22 in Marrakech, the spotlight was cast on the critical need to adapt African agriculture to the challenges posed by climate change. In response, the Moroccan government, together with the World Bank, committed to facilitating the creation of a series of 'Climate Smart Agriculture Investment Plans (\",\"_key\":\"a562a6240e390\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"d7f9dd0811e6\"],\"text\":\"CSAIPs\",\"_key\":\"a562a6240e391\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"). These plans aim to pinpoint actionable strategies that governments can adopt to enhance climate-smart agriculture. This includes identifying opportunities for investment as well as designing and implementing relevant policies.\",\"_key\":\"a562a6240e392\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"0c72a64c0d9e\"},{\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"7499c93141a4\",\"markDefs\":[{\"href\":\"https://journals.plos.org/plosone/article?id=10.1371/journal.pone.0234213\",\"_key\":\"2e83d0f41b25\",\"_type\":\"link\"},{\"href\":\"https://cgspace.cgiar.org/bitstreams/6c3bb7cf-eeee-4024-945a-569f31690b12/download\",\"_key\":\"c65d8534d6cf\",\"_type\":\"link\"}],\"children\":[{\"text\":\"Data from the Atlas was indispensable for developing CSAIPs in four countries. Atlas analysis provided information to identify the risks and help prioritize investment opportunities including a comprehensive compilation of climate-related data, including detailed analyses of upcoming hazards, the extent of agricultural exposure, similarly to the data in the Spotlight, “What’s at Risk”.\",\"_key\":\"87ca49247cc1\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}],\"_type\":\"block\"},{\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"acf07ab81767\",\"markDefs\":[{\"href\":\"https://journals.plos.org/plosone/article?id=10.1371/journal.pone.0234213\",\"_key\":\"2e83d0f41b25\",\"_type\":\"link\"},{\"_type\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://cgspace.cgiar.org/bitstreams/6c3bb7cf-eeee-4024-945a-569f31690b12/download\",\"_key\":\"c65d8534d6cf\"}],\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"d2a9bac6ebee\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Uniquely the Atlas was able to also provide information on the economics of many adaptation options, which will later be highlighted in a forthcoming Spotlight, “Economics of Adaptation”. This critical data was used as an input into cost-benefit models (\"},{\"text\":\"Yet et al.\",\"_key\":\"8d744325b1751\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"2e83d0f41b25\"]},{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"; \",\"_key\":\"8d744325b1752\",\"_type\":\"span\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"c65d8534d6cf\"],\"text\":\"Rosenstock et al.\",\"_key\":\"8d744325b1753\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\") and helped stakeholder understand the potential costs and benefits of various options. This economic rationale was pivotal in securing buy-in from governments, donors, and the private sector, each of which plays a critical role in scaling up adaptation.\",\"_key\":\"8d744325b1754\"}],\"_type\":\"block\"}],\"_id\":\"46f5919a-ce13-4f10-9f4b-6f3a56828882\",\"_type\":\"impact\",\"title\":\"The AAA Initiative and partners developed national investment plans using Atlas data\"},{\"comingSoon\":true,\"slug\":\"identify-common-climate-threats \",\"content\":[{\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"lorem ipsom\",\"_key\":\"3f5ae9e2fb25\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"7be7c8906430\"}],\"featuredTags\":[{\"slug\":{\"current\":\"hazards\",\"_type\":\"slug\"},\"_id\":\"d4f0b388-28d1-4707-86cb-3c89d9903357\",\"name\":\"Hazards\"},{\"name\":\"Exposure\",\"slug\":{\"_type\":\"slug\",\"current\":\"exposure\"},\"_id\":\"91d5bc42-a1ce-4f74-89c5-ef4c6489eb44\"},{\"_id\":\"9cb49d42-59b2-4625-89e5-b8355518cdbd\",\"name\":\"Risk\",\"slug\":{\"current\":\"risk\",\"_type\":\"slug\"}}],\"primaryTags\":[{\"slug\":{\"current\":\"hazards\",\"_type\":\"slug\"},\"_id\":\"d4f0b388-28d1-4707-86cb-3c89d9903357\",\"name\":\"Hazards\"},{\"slug\":{\"current\":\"exposure\",\"_type\":\"slug\"},\"_id\":\"91d5bc42-a1ce-4f74-89c5-ef4c6489eb44\",\"name\":\"Exposure\"},{\"_id\":\"9cb49d42-59b2-4625-89e5-b8355518cdbd\",\"name\":\"Risk\",\"slug\":{\"_type\":\"slug\",\"current\":\"risk\"}}],\"_id\":\"9ef68f07-ffbb-488f-8151-ed33e45f5bd1\",\"_type\":\"spotlight\",\"title\":\"Identify Common Climate Threats \"},{\"_type\":\"impact\",\"title\":\"Our data can help NGOs, researchers, governments, international finance institutions, and you, too. It’s free. Start here.\",\"slug\":\"our-data-can-help\",\"content\":[{\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Robust and Timely Data\",\"_key\":\"5ebb3a7f7fe10\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"f15985d8f467\",\"markDefs\":[]},{\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"fc15f1782b42\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"We have assembled data on a range of topics related to agriculture and climate change in Sub-Saharan Africa as a resource for approaching adaptation projects. This includes data and projections on climate change impacts, economic risks, adaptive capacities, effective adaptation practices and strategies, investment returns, and more. This rich source of insights can help create actionable decision-making support for investment design, policy formulation, development programming, and other use cases related to adaptation in agriculture.\",\"_key\":\"6d69141070ff0\"}]},{\"alt\":\"Soil sampling. Communities in Lushuto are taught how to dig a basic soil profile to enable a basic \\\"diagnostic\\\".\",\"caption\":[{\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"8e3184c23527\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"strong\"],\"text\":\"Image credit:\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" ©2014CIAT/GeorginaSmith\",\"_key\":\"30431aece315\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"dec2baf02afb\",\"markDefs\":[]}],\"_key\":\"8ebf9d20a047\",\"asset\":{\"_type\":\"reference\",\"_ref\":\"image-fcaee318efb5605479fa5c53f1dab346c3c130c6-4288x2848-jpg\"},\"_type\":\"imageFull\"},{\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"e17b2af170c6\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"How People Are Using Our Data\",\"_key\":\"42b8a5ee94920\"}],\"_type\":\"block\"},{\"_key\":\"29ca0473808d\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Our data has helped many organizations further their work, such as the IUCN, World Bank, United States Department of Agriculture, IFPRI, IITA, Kenyan Ministry of Agriculture, CGIAR, and Alliance of Bioversity-CIAT.\",\"_key\":\"fb6482799a220\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\"},{\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"ab9227d961a2\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"NGOs, researchers, governments, international finance institutions, and other groups are using the Atlas data in many ways, including:\",\"_key\":\"75f7f39c24390\"}],\"_type\":\"block\"},{\"markDefs\":[{\"_key\":\"3e0ea4566336\",\"_type\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://adaptationatlas.cgiar.org/data-in-practice/iucn-gcf\"}],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Developing clear reasoning and justification to shape Green Climate Fund proposals. \",\"_key\":\"1e4ea3da1a880\",\"_type\":\"span\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"3e0ea4566336\"],\"text\":\"Case study\",\"_key\":\"1e4ea3da1a881\"}],\"level\":1,\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"2481824cf299\",\"listItem\":\"bullet\"},{\"_key\":\"9ec613b40d05\",\"listItem\":\"bullet\",\"markDefs\":[{\"_type\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://adaptationatlas.cgiar.org/data-in-practice/world-bank-aiccra\",\"_key\":\"a3307cf0d80c\"}],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Generating key economic performance indicators to support investor decisions. \",\"_key\":\"e90dc1b9f20d0\",\"_type\":\"span\"},{\"marks\":[\"a3307cf0d80c\"],\"text\":\"Case study\",\"_key\":\"e90dc1b9f20d1\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"level\":1,\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\"},{\"listItem\":\"bullet\",\"markDefs\":[{\"_type\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://adaptationatlas.cgiar.org/data-in-practice/aaa-csaips\",\"_key\":\"3f8a4151a411\"}],\"children\":[{\"text\":\"Outlining adaptation rationale and response options in four African countries. \",\"_key\":\"bb23569605430\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"3f8a4151a411\"],\"text\":\"Case study\",\"_key\":\"bb23569605431\"}],\"level\":1,\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"6507712c6cf8\"},{\"level\":1,\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"3e4876c44373\",\"listItem\":\"bullet\",\"markDefs\":[{\"_type\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://adaptationatlas.cgiar.org/data-in-practice/government-kenya\",\"_key\":\"d22f52c3c046\"}],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Formulating evidence-based climate change response plans. \",\"_key\":\"9dcc862c8be20\",\"_type\":\"span\"},{\"marks\":[\"d22f52c3c046\"],\"text\":\"Case study\",\"_key\":\"9dcc862c8be21\",\"_type\":\"span\"}]},{\"level\":1,\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"ceaba934c2ed\",\"listItem\":\"bullet\",\"markDefs\":[{\"_type\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://adaptationatlas.cgiar.org/data-in-practice/cgiar-strategy\",\"_key\":\"0c26fa574a1e\"}],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Supporting projections of climate risks and adaptation benefits for prioritizing research. \",\"_key\":\"707e6885376b0\",\"_type\":\"span\"},{\"text\":\"Case study\",\"_key\":\"707e6885376b1\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"0c26fa574a1e\"]}]},{\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"0ef5a40f1daa\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"text\":\"A Collaborative Platform for Our Data and Yours\",\"_key\":\"d60031c1137b0\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}]},{\"_key\":\"0b016e847fcd\",\"markDefs\":[{\"_type\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://observablehq.com/collection/@adaptationatlas/data-spotlights\",\"_key\":\"b9cb30e6fcac\"}],\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"4dd9b618efa20\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Building effective adaptation solutions is a collaborative process, and making data usable for more stakeholders can expedite and amplify those efforts. This is why we have utilized \"},{\"marks\":[\"b9cb30e6fcac\"],\"text\":\"Observable\",\"_key\":\"4dd9b618efa21\",\"_type\":\"span\"},{\"text\":\", a collaborative platform for data exploration and visualization, to build a growing collection of tools for visually exploring our data, and to facilitate stakeholders in building tools for the collection using their own data. This is a community effort aimed at supporting people working in all aspects of adaptation agriculture. Have an idea or need for a specific data tool that can bring information to a key decision? Reach out for support or follow our Guidelines to:\",\"_key\":\"4dd9b618efa22\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\"},{\"_key\":\"f13e376aee5f\",\"listItem\":\"bullet\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"415d5fc2dfeb0\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Use our data to create new tools\"}],\"level\":1,\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\"},{\"_key\":\"e60fc676264f\",\"listItem\":\"bullet\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"1f85c66deaa40\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Duplicate and modify our existing tools\"}],\"level\":1,\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\"},{\"listItem\":\"bullet\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Use new data to create new tools\",\"_key\":\"0947db4b85100\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"level\":1,\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"345c992eb120\"},{\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"087db05e830c\",\"markDefs\":[{\"href\":\"mailto: toddrosenstock@adaptationatlas.info\",\"_key\":\"2d5fcc7bae26\",\"_type\":\"link\"}],\"children\":[{\"text\":\"Do you have data that could complement the Atlas but need help putting your data into practice? Our team might be able to help. \",\"_key\":\"bceb902e09460\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]},{\"_key\":\"bceb902e09461\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"2d5fcc7bae26\"],\"text\":\"Let us know\"},{\"_key\":\"bceb902e09462\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" and we can discuss incorporating it into the Atlas.\"}]},{\"_key\":\"486b77031d42\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Access the Data\",\"_key\":\"8f2c362bffe40\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\"},{\"children\":[{\"text\":\"We encourage the use of our data and data visualizations in your work. Data used throughout the Atlas is available through our online \",\"_key\":\"2da0d82d9d8e0\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[]},{\"marks\":[\"d95b9f3cbc3b\"],\"text\":\"SpatioTemporal Asset Catalog\",\"_key\":\"2da0d82d9d8e1\",\"_type\":\"span\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" (STAC). Download part or all based on your needs. We also created The Explore the Datasets Observable Notebook (Coming soon) to provide access to key data layers from the Adaptation Atlas site and suite of notebooks. In most notebooks, data used for specific visualizations can be downloaded directly from the Observable page in the top right of the browser window (look for the paperclip ‘file attachments’). Data sources and methodology vary between notebooks and detailed information (with links to \",\"_key\":\"2da0d82d9d8e2\"},{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[\"c15f20aca273\"],\"text\":\"Github\",\"_key\":\"2da0d82d9d8e3\"},{\"marks\":[],\"text\":\" with our code) can be found in the Methods \\u0026 Sources at the end of the notebooks.\",\"_key\":\"2da0d82d9d8e4\",\"_type\":\"span\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"bf355be373e1\",\"markDefs\":[{\"_key\":\"d95b9f3cbc3b\",\"_type\":\"link\",\"href\":\"https://radiantearth.github.io/stac-browser/#/external/digital-atlas.s3.amazonaws.com/stac/public_stac/catalog.json\"},{\"href\":\"https://github.com/AdaptationAtlas\",\"_key\":\"c15f20aca273\",\"_type\":\"link\"}]},{\"children\":[{\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Get in Touch\",\"_key\":\"f7431ee7835a0\"}],\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"h2\",\"_key\":\"7f85cee52741\",\"markDefs\":[]},{\"_type\":\"block\",\"style\":\"normal\",\"_key\":\"456cd762f313\",\"markDefs\":[],\"children\":[{\"_key\":\"5d3df0df53640\",\"_type\":\"span\",\"marks\":[],\"text\":\"Are you using data from the Atlas now? Let us know. We’d love to feature your work here and make it available for others in the community. Please contact us if you have any questions, would like to contribute new information to the Atlas, provide feedback, or request to be put on our mailing list.\"}]}],\"_id\":\"bad166ef-e62b-4db1-be49-57af0849ef6e\"}],\"ms\":48}"
          },
